re/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T14:00:19-08:00","id":6314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=2626#post2626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a fan of Type Moon. Nasu's writingg doesn't do it for me</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, from what I understand a lot of &quot;Nasu's writing&quot; comes from an awkwardly literal translation into English.<br /> <br /> As for recommendations :<br /> - <b>Slayers </b>(Fantasy/Adventures anime based on a light novel written by Hajime Kanzaka and illustrated by Rui Araizumi)<br /> - <b>Gunnm </b>(Sci-Fi Seinen manga) and its sequel <b>Gunnm Last Order</b><br /> - <b>Hellsing </b>(Horror Seinen manga/anime/OVA)<br /> - <b>Tenchi Muyo! OVAs</b> (original Harem accept no substitutes) and its sequel<b> Isekai no Seikishi Monogatari</b><br /> - <b>Black Lagoon</b> (Action/comedy Seinen manga &amp; anime)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://oi61.tinypic.com/30cn5ug.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> A.K.A. Xelloss33","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/924-xelloss","name":"Xelloss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar924_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T23:49:15-08:00","id":6668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xelloss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=6314#post6314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, from what I understand a lot of &quot;Nasu's writing&quot; comes from an awkwardly literal translation into English.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about the translations really. I'm talking about his actual writing. He has a really bad habit of dragging me right out of the moment. He writes too much exposition about one thing in the middle of events, for my liking. I just don't care for Type Moon. Not my thing. I'm an Age guy. KimiNozu, Muv Luv, KimiIta. Those all do it for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:37:51-08:00","id":7532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=5223#post5223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the manga is excellent for watamote. The show is pretty good too. That's the OP for all the episode IIRC. She's not really misanthropic as much as she is an awkward pervert otaku with no friends. It can get hard to read and watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit you were not kidding. I am ten minutes in. This is intensely and uncomfortably familiar.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Five episodes in. This is heartbreaking. Comedic at times, but stunningly bleak and nihilistic at its core. Definitely going to keep watching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 11-10-2013, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T22:14:59-08:00","id":7880,"title":"","content":"Cerealkiller: As my pm's somehow end up having an empty text I'll write it here:<br /> <br /> I had asked if you also include indie VNs in your VN list.<br /> <br /> If so then as example:<br /> <a href=\"http://lemmasoft.renai.us/forums/viewforum.php?f=11&amp;amp;sid=54fdaf33169eedd155be2f0\" target=\"_blank\">http://lemmasoft.renai.us/forums/vie...69eedd155be2f0</a> 3ca6eaf7f<br /> <br /> That is a site for indie VNs (to be exact it is a site for indie vn game developers who talk about problems, hire staff but also who publish their games there. Most of the games are cost free which affects the quaility of about 70% of the VNs published there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T01:19:40-08:00","id":7928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=7880#post7880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cerealkiller: As my pm's somehow end up having an empty text I'll write it here:<br /> <br /> I had asked if you also include indie VNs in your VN list.<br /> <br /> If so then as example:<br /> <a href=\"http://lemmasoft.renai.us/forums/viewforum.php?f=11&amp;amp;sid=54fdaf33169eedd155be2f0\" target=\"_blank\">http://lemmasoft.renai.us/forums/vie...69eedd155be2f0</a> 3ca6eaf7f<br /> <br /> That is a site for indie VNs (to be exact it is a site for indie vn game developers who talk about problems, hire staff but also who publish their games there. Most of the games are cost free which affects the quaility of about 70% of the VNs published there).</div> </div> </div> </div>are the VNs OEL (original English Language)? I've found that most OELs don't do it for me. Something is always off or just bothers me. Or they feel too fan-fictiony. The only one I read that I thought was okay, and is probably the best written, drawn and everything OEL VN, is Katawa Shoujo. i only read 3 routes but those routes were okay.<br /> <br /> Speaking of VNs my best friend and another friend are both done with their editing of Sumaga from JAST. I'm re-reading muv luv right now which may seem like a torturous thing to do but I'm thinking of stopping when I finish extra again and just leave it be. I've got Altered Fable so I'm hoping to see the translation make more progress again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T02:37:39-08:00","id":7941,"title":"","content":"Most are original english language VNs. A handful are japanese or multilanguage ones. I think about 80 or even 90% have original stories (varying in how good they are storywise still) and the other 10-20% are fanfictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:33:32-08:00","id":8145,"title":"","content":"I do think its really cool. I want to see an actually good and well written OEL come out. tbh I want it to be voiced but I want Japanese talent not US/UK talent because those who are usually in the dubbing industry tend to overact or underact or mess up the voices etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:53:07-08:00","id":8896,"title":"","content":"Finished Watamote. That was the most accurate depiction of depression and loneliness I've ever seen. Hope comes in fits and starts, followed soon after by disappointment, sliding downward to a tearful period of crisis and recovery - and then the cycle starts again. No cliche lessons here. I just want to reach into my screen and give Tomoko a hug.<br /> <br /> And I'd probably also tell her that it's totally okay to be into girls. I mean seriously, every time Yuu shows up there's lesbian subtext through the roof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T17:44:57-08:00","id":13709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=7532#post7532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Holy shit you were not kidding. I am ten minutes in. This is intensely and uncomfortably familiar.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Five episodes in. This is heartbreaking. Comedic at times, but stunningly bleak and nihilistic at its core. Definitely going to keep watching.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of a thing I said to a friend about it back in July:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> this show makes me super uncomfortable i can't wait to watch it every week for three months </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:08:57-08:00","id":16324,"title":"","content":"<i>Samurai Flamenco</i> just upended my expectations about the show with the ending of episode #7: as I watched the last scene, I was having trouble believing that it wasn\u2019t intended to be a dream sequence. But the way it ended, it looks like the writers are serious about this latest plot twist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T15:21:10-08:00","id":20395,"title":"","content":"Two of my favorites most won't think about or have even seen.<br /> <br /> Shiki (Basically Salem's Lot Anime), Karin(Reverse Vampire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T21:36:27-08:00","id":20498,"title":"","content":"Seen em both. If you want another good vampire anime check out Kurozuka.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T22:42:27-08:00","id":20512,"title":"","content":"I actually got around to watching Shiki a couple months ago. It was a lot of fun. The buildup from episodes 1-12 was a little slow, and there was a definite formula going on that started to get a tad old, but once the ball got rolling, it really rolled. I do wish the cast of characters had been a little smaller, so that they could have spent a bit more time developing some of them, but it's a pretty small complaint all told. It also had the most <i>fabulous</i> hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T23:35:11-08:00","id":20519,"title":"","content":"itsuka tenma no kuro usagi had maybe the best hair ever. gradient beautiful hair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T00:06:31-08:00","id":21031,"title":"","content":"There's another series that the same artist works on (he's Brazilian) called No Game, No Life. <a href=\"http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2013-07-28/no-game-no-life-light-novels-by-itsuten-kamiya-gets-anime\" target=\"_blank\">It's getting an anime series this next year</a> so stay tuned for more amazing gradient hair. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T08:32:34-08:00","id":25128,"title":"","content":"Madoka Magica Rebellion was phenomenal, and even scarier, it's made the case that Madoka Magica on the whole could be a perfect story. It was fucking amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T08:55:41-08:00","id":25141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=25128#post25128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Madoka Magica Rebellion was phenomenal, and even scarier, it's made the case that Madoka Magica on the whole could be a perfect story. It was fucking amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to go with a couple of friends but couldn't because of work. Well I say they are friends, more like casual acquaintances. They both