lue":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T09:18:46-08:00","id":29948,"title":"","content":"Cereal. I think I remember you mentioning you were playing Kancolle? How was it? Anything you noted? It seems to be getting popular and I was thinking of giving it a try. Wanted to know what you thought about it first though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T20:49:01-08:00","id":30255,"title":"","content":"Its hard as HELL to get into it. they only open it up for about 5000 people at a time every once in a while at like 5AM EST. its a pretty neat game. You go on expeditions with your ships and work your way up from destroyers and light cruisers to heavy cruisers and battleships and aircraft carriers. I'm buying ALL of the ships and kits. The art is excellent and the voice talent is top notch. For instance: Kuma class light cruisers are voiced by Marina Inuoe (Yozora from Haganai). Nao Touyama (Kanon from The World God Only Knows) also voices some of the heavy cruisers IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T05:10:53-08:00","id":33797,"title":"","content":"You guys, Kill la Kill is just <i>so good</i> you guys, like you wouldn't even believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T11:55:23-08:00","id":33995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=33797#post33797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys, Kill la Kill is just <i>so good</i> you guys, like you wouldn't even believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I would believe. Because I watch it every week. It's easily my second favorite show this season (and in any other season would be number one, it just has the bad luck to be in the same season as Monogatari). <br /> <br /> The characters are all really fun, Mako especially. Even the new character Nui was quite entertaining. I can't wait to see where the storyline goes from here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T12:11:06-08:00","id":34003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=33995#post33995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The characters are all really fun, Mako especially.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Mako really came into her own in this episode. I am so amazingly gratified for the fact that, for all her goofy fun, she can be up on what's going on when it matters.<br /> <br /> I also really want to see where Satsuki's going, which extends into the fact that there's some stuff thus far only hinted at (for a show that began as this one did, it's got a surprising grasp at subtlety in storytelling).<br /> <br /> To whit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the new character Nui was quite entertaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the character in her own right, but I mostly like what she reveals or implies about other characters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T23:16:58-08:00","id":47963,"title":"","content":"So, the new season started a couple weeks ago. Here's a quick list of what I'm watching and enjoying.<br /> <br /> Wizard Barristers seems pretty interesting. It's a &quot;modern world + magic&quot; setting. The main character is working as a lawyer for people caught breaking the law through the use of magic. It seems like mages have their own court system, which tends towards extremely harsh punishments. It's clear that mages, due to the power they have, face fear and discrimination. Fairly interesting first episode. I'm curious to see where it goes. <br /> <br /> Sekai Seifuku - The MC joins a group (led by a little girl) bent on conquering the world using magic and monsters. It seems there's going to be magical girls opposing them. I think I'll stick with it. It seems like it will be amusing, if only because of the &quot;reversed&quot; role, of the MC being part of the world conquering &quot;villains.&quot;<br /> <br /> Saki - The Nationals. More mahjong fun. I know nothing about mahjong, but for some reason I enjoyed the heck out of the first two seasons. <br /> <br /> Chuunibyou Season 2 - Continuation of the series that was running last year. More of the same hijinks and such. Fun enough.<br /> <br /> Space Dandy - I like the animation and the characters are all quite entertaining.<br /> <br /> There's two series involving Nobunaga out. I haven't had the chance to watch them yet; might give it a shot next week. <br /> <br /> Anybody else watching anything they like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T06:51:13-08:00","id":48130,"title":"","content":"I've yet to get a chance to watch anything yet but Robot Girls Z but my watch list for this season is:<br /> Gundam Build Fighters<br /> Nagi No Asukara<br /> Strike the Blood (just picking it up)<br /> Log Horizon (just picking it up)<br /> Yusuha ni Narenakatta (picking up now from last season)<br /> White Album 2 (piccking up now from last season)<br /> Walkure Romanze (picking up now from last season)<br /> Arpegggio (picking up now from last season)<br /> Non Non Biyori (heard this was really funny, going to give it a few episodes)<br /> Outbreak Company (just picking up)<br /> <br /> This Season:<br /> Robot Girls Z<br /> Nisekoi<br /> Space Dandy<br /> Sakura Trick<br /> Strange+<br /> Nourin<br /> Saki S3<br /> Wake Up Girls<br /> Witch Craft Works (maybe)<br /> Chuu2Koi S2<br /> Majokko movie (sounds cute)<br /> Lupin III v Detective Conan Movie<br /> Mouretsu Pirates movie<br /> idolm@ster movie","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T07:34:46-08:00","id":48154,"title":"","content":"I think you might like Non Non Biyori. It was my third favorite show last season. One of the better slow-paced slice of life's I've seen in few years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-14-2014, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:35:23-08:00","id":53512,"title":"","content":"In this season, there's Mahou Sensou (Magic Warfare), too. The plot is really similar to Mage TA and I think someone who know the game can enjoy the anime (or be outraged) :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:20:29-08:00","id":54817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=53512#post53512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this season, there's Mahou Sensou (Magic Warfare), too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watched the first two episodes last night. It wasn't bad (other than the guy with the bamboo shinai somehow blocking a hundred attacks from the guy wielding the 20 pound sharp metal sword) and the fact that we had a character who looked a lot like Gilgamesh, a character who looked a lot like Saber, a character who looked a lot like Lancer (only with red hair) and a character who looks just like Shana from Shakugan no Shana.<br /> <br /> I think I'll keep watching it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T14:37:26-08:00","id":54913,"title":"","content":"In the veing that I'm perpetually behind everything, I finished Ga Rei Zero last week and found it immensely satisfying save for the fact it's a prequel,so certain things just don't have closure. Highly recommend it if you're into simple relationships and subtle build up and payoffs int regards to the dyanmics of those relationships peppered with awesome and implausible fighting.<br /> <br /> On a different tangent though, I'm starting to get to the point where, between this and Fate Zero, where I wish that there was a way these people who do awesome prequels to mediocre stories could just come up with their own ending. It's impossible, but man there are quite a few prequel stories that would have been better if they weren't bound to the future events of the series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:57:45-08:00","id":56269,"title":"","content":"I've been watching &quot;Attack on Titan&quot;. Kind of cool. A little annoying at times though because people seem to become stupid just to move the plot in certain directions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T01:25:44-08:00","id":57981,"title":"","content":"So, the Full Metal Panic Sigma manga ended, which also ended the series. Great ending, great series. I am a little sad it ended though; I've been following it for 12 years now. That's a pretty long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T09:41:01-08:00","id":60848,"title":"","content":"Is it weird that hearing about the infamous &quot;Endless Eight&quot; story arc kinda makes me want to watch it myself just to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T09:58:32-08:00","id":60865,"title":"","content":"If you haven't already seen the first season of Haruhi, you probably should. While it wasn't a terribly amazing amazing, it is a rather popular and influential series. You see lots of references to it constantly. And if you've seen it and liked it, then you might as well check out the second season (of which Endless 8 is a big part) which some people enjoyed and others hated. It was an interesting experiment, but I totally understand why people who were watching it as it came out, were very upset. If you don't know what you're getting into, then yeah, you pry won't like it. It works a lot better when you can just grab the episodes and watch them all at once, rather than having to watch 1 episode each week expecting something to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-29-2014, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:40:32-08:00","id":60904,"title":"","content":"I get the same sort of feeling in regards to School Days, Cielle, but Anubis is right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T12:42:20-08:00","id":60992,"title":"","content":"I know Gatchaman Crowds has been out for a while, and I'm only watching it intermittently, but I still think it's worth saying how it continues to pleasantly surprise me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T16:27:57-08:00","id":62546,"title":"","content":"So, I started watching Birdy the Mighty: Decode. Aside from Birdy's and some other characters rather skimpy outfits, it doesn't really focus on fanservice the way some other animes with barely dressed action girls tend to do. Seems to be a good sci-fi/Superhero cartoon with Japanese flavor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T10:46:22-08:00","id":62992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=60992#post60992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Gatchaman Crowds has been out for a while, and I'm only watching it intermittently, but I still think it's worth saying how it continues to pleasantly surprise me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gatchaman was fun. I had a lot of trouble predicting where things would go, and everytime I thought I had figured it out, Hajime would run off and do something else. I'm glad she wasn't a player in an RPG campaign I ran; predicting her actions would be impossible.<br /> <br /> Make sure to grab the director's cut. The ending of the series was rushed, and the director's cut fills in the gaps so you actually know what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:30:04-08:00","id":64210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=60992#post60992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Gatchaman Crowds has been out for a while, and I'm only watching it intermittently, but I still think it's worth saying how it continues to pleasantly surprise me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only seen the first episode, but the whole time I'm thinking that the Gatchaman name just seems to be a cruch. It like what Hollywood keeps doing, why use the name if it really has nothing to do with the series it is named after?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:07:35-08:00","id":64248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=62992#post62992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">everytime I thought I had figured it out, Hajime would run off and do something else. I'm glad she wasn't a player in an RPG campaign I ran; predicting her actions would be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like Hajime. I like how she's kind of flighty and quirky, but also insightful and well-meaning, how she's not in awe of characters who she should be subordinate to or are kind of godlike, but in a wholly good-natured and friendly way rather than some kind of directionless defiance, and how she keeps questioning the premise as it's presented to her rather than just blindly following along with it, and trying to reach out to the things she's on the opposite side of.<br /> <br /> Within the first three episodes, I was really won over by the way that she was pleasantly insistent on being told exactly <i>why</i> they need to fight these aliens, and a few episodes later when she asks exactly why Gatchaman need to be kept secret, just because I'd usually feel a sense of dissatisfaction of how many similar characters either wouldn't bring it up or accept the first answer they're given.<br /> <br /> Like, the social media angle was the thing that shook me of my first episode notion that the show had nothing to distinguish itself, but Hajime's a big part of why I'm actually invested.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:40:29-08:00","id":64281,"title":"","content":"One thing I really liked about Gatchaman was Rui.<br /> <br /> Minor spoilers ahead (though nothing plot related.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Normally anime has a pretty poor track record with transgendered or transvestite characters. Usually they're only there for comic relief, and have a five o'clock shadow and a feather boa. I liked how with Rui, the fact that she was a guy who wore girls clothing wasn't a thing. Nobody really mentioned it, thought about it or cared. It's not often you see that in anime, and that, plus Hajime's attitude, really won me over to the show. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T08:30:08-08:00","id":65714,"title":"","content":"I'm watching Chaos;Head. So far it is ok. Seems like it is trying too hard to be cerebral. Ego Proxy light.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T08:40:05-08:00","id":65719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=65714#post65714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm watching Chaos;Head. So far it is ok. Seems like it is trying too hard to be cerebral. Ego Proxy light.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGood luck to ya! I started watching, feeling a certain Ergo Proxy meets Paranoia Agent vibe (Woo-hoo! Right!?!), but by the end...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The end was bad. And stupid. And stupidly bad. I realize that's just my opinion, but...yeah. Awful. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank