and then enjoy me some Last Exile after it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T23:05:18-07:00","id":109009,"title":"","content":"I thought Rebellion was... okay. Not a terribly big fan of it. The first half of the movie felt like it was just filler, and it took a long while to start getting interesting. Once it did, it was good, but it took way to long to get to that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T10:48:29-07:00","id":109439,"title":"","content":"I hear that a lot, and I get where they're coming from, but the big thing for me is that that first part informs the final part(you know what I'm talking). The similarity between the two confirms the reasons and the ideas at work in case people missed the massive buildup throughout the entire series to that point(and beyond it). It is important to establishing perfect(or near perfect, or at least better, depending on who you are) clarity.<br /> <br /> I bring this up namely because it seems like most people(Not you, Anubis) I read talking about the opening also have problems with the sharp turn of the ending.<br /> <br /> As for it's pacing, asides from what they have to cram in there, admittedly, it almost felt too long for me. THe gears shifted right when I was starting to go &quot;Okay, stop lying to me&quot;, which is actually a really good time to do so, if not perfect(and clearly it was for some, hence our conversation). For me it worked out.<br /> <br /> My final thing on the beginning is just that I loved the homage as well as the fan skewering. All talk of &quot;the opening explains the ending&quot; aside, it is fanservice-y...but for me, not in a bad way. I love the nods to the genre and the loving acknowledgment of it-it was like the guys at Shaft and in the Quartet were trying to say that they really did like magical girls and all the standard things about it even if they were then going to proceed to rip it all a new one. Urobuchi said he wasn't deliberately deconstructing the genre, and even if he is lying,I liked how this felt like a nod to the fact that he had still done just that by giving the normal presentation of the genre its' dues.<br /> <br /> The fan-skewering was also great-I'm sorry, but I have this horrible thing where I love the audience getting slapped(playfully or lovingly, or at least parentally, rather than malevolently or spitefully, BURTON) by the creators, and the opening also did that. It positively <i>rolled around</i> in fan stories and opinions and gleefully covered itself in fan culture like a pig in mud, and then looked at the audience and asked &quot;Now come on, did you <i>really</i> think your stories would actually work?&quot; with a big mischievous grin on its' face. It went on just long enough and with the right tone that I wasn't really that bothered by it.<br /> <br /> WARNING: The spoiler doesn't give away specific details, but it does allude to the nature of the ending which will of course somewhat inform your viewing if you haven't seen the movie yet. I don't think it hurts knowing the nature of the ending in the sense I'm talking about(as people might get a sour taste in their mouth otherwise), but just in case I put it in spoilers. Just being cautious, I'm speaking in the vaguest of terms, but it does allude to a definitive quality of the ending. That said, it does inform the main reason I like Rebellion, which has less to do with itself and more to do with Madoka on the whole.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Of course, the big reason I like this movie is that while it is anywhere from a good-if-at-times-tiring film to a really solid piece on the whole(and I am in the latter, as you can tell), it's what it does for the whole of the series. It clearly needs the final installation for me to say anything concrete, but it's natural progression of and challenge to the ideas at work really elevate what the series is asking and semi-answering, and they way it does that just about nears perfection on the technical grounds.<br /> <br /> It's not what I would call the best(that goes with all my bias to Utena), but the Rebellion took an already impresively told story and took it just about the pinnacle of actual story craft. What it does it greater than what it is, is what I'm saying.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T12:12:30-07:00","id":109526,"title":"","content":"Yeah with Rebellion -<br /> <br /> Spoilers in here so read at your own risk<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I enjoyed the ending. I thought it was perfect. That was always my problem with the original series. Homura is revealed to be the &quot;main&quot; character, and she got kind of shafted at the end. She never gets her wish granted. So I enjoyed what Rebellion added to the story and that we got to see her get her wish, even if it came at the expense of everyone else. But I've always dug that type of storyline.<br /> <br /> I just thought the rest of the movie was a bit weak. The initial setting where they're fighting the nightmares didn't feel too important. You had the &quot;cake-song&quot; scene. You had some other miscellaneous scenes. I was really getting a bit bored until Homura and Kyouko went on their trip. That was, for all intents and purposes, when the story actually started, and even that scene dragged on a bit too long. I think they could have taken all the above and compressed it down into 10 minutes; it felt like it was just there to fill out the movie.<br /> <br /> That said I did like Bebe. She was pretty cool.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-p-WXyscT6YA/U0WaKubAXOI/AAAAAAAAAVA/9Cq6kqoKAMQ/w245-h138-no/1396335288415.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T13:16:43-07:00","id":109580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=109526#post109526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah with Rebellion -<br /> <br /> Spoilers in here so read at your own risk<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I enjoyed the ending. I thought it was perfect. That was always my problem with the original series. Homura is revealed to be the &quot;main&quot; character, and she got kind of shafted at the end. She never gets her wish granted. So I enjoyed what Rebellion added to the story and that we got to see her get her wish, even if it came at the expense of everyone else. But I've always dug that type of storyline.<br /> <br /> I just thought the rest of the movie was a bit weak. The initial setting where they're fighting the nightmares didn't feel too important. You had the &quot;cake-song&quot; scene. You had some other miscellaneous scenes. I was really getting a bit bored until Homura and Kyouko went on their trip. That was, for all intents and purposes, when the story actually started, and even that scene dragged on a bit too long. I think they could have taken all the above and compressed it down into 10 minutes; it felt like it was just there to fill out the movie.<br /> <br /> That said I did like Bebe. She was pretty cool.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-p-WXyscT6YA/U0WaKubAXOI/AAAAAAAAAVA/9Cq6kqoKAMQ/w245-h138-no/1396335288415.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, I got the impression that you liked the ending. And yes, the story changes gears...actually a little earlier than that, right after the Hitomi Nightmare fight, but it doesn't settle into fully doing so until Homura begins asking Kyoko questions. And yeah, from right after to the Hitomi fight to when Homura finally puts on the old badass persona(and begins the wonderful montage that is her dramatic hair that we call the movie) is slower than it needs to be.<br /> <br /> But once again, The opening is what completes the justification of Homucifer's reality rewrite. Her curse/wish is realized, perhaps even more fully than she recognizes now, in that opening sequence-that is what Homura wants. It sets the stage for when she creates her own fantasy, and even the series beyond that by showing what she wants and what she thinks she wants(granted, the second is more informed by the others persona's and reaction to the grand picture, but that doesn't stop it from not really being what she wants). So between that and the fanservice/skewering as well as the squeezed in just right pacing for me, I don't have the same issue with the opening everyone else does. I get why people do, and given the wiggle room of subjectivity in art it's worth noting they are right(enough, says the back of my mind), but I'm at the other end of that wiggle room.<br /> <br /> The cake song is weird though. I'm lacking a context to find that anything but straight up weird.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Nagisa is actually someone I worried about going in, but she was handled well enough. She was fun without being over stated. And yeah that gif is cuterrifying.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T23:30:03-07:00","id":109887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=109580#post109580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, I got the impression that you liked the ending. And yes, the story changes gears...actually a little earlier than that, right after the Hitomi Nightmare fight, but it doesn't settle into fully doing so until Homura begins asking Kyoko questions. And yeah, from right after to the Hitomi fight to when Homura finally puts on the old badass persona(and begins the wonderful montage that is her dramatic hair that we call the movie) is slower than it needs to be.<br /> <br /> But once again, The opening is what completes the justification of Homucifer's reality rewrite. Her curse/wish is realized, perhaps even more fully than she recognizes now, in that opening sequence-that is what Homura wants. It sets the stage for when she creates her own fantasy, and even the series beyond that by showing what she wants and what she thinks she wants(granted, the second is more informed by the others persona's and reaction to the grand picture, but that doesn't stop it from not really being what she wants). So between that and the fanservice/skewering as well as the squeezed in just right pacing for me, I don't have the same issue with the opening everyone else does. I get why people do, and given the wiggle room of subjectivity in art it's worth noting they are right(enough, says the back of my mind), but I'm at the other end of that wiggle room.<br /> <br /> The cake song is weird though. I'm lacking a context to find that anything but straight up weird.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Nagisa is actually someone I worried about going in, but she was handled well enough. She was fun without being over stated. And yeah that gif is cuterrifying.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, when I heard that they were adding in a new character I thought, &quot;Oh brother,&quot; and rolled my eyes. But she was pretty inoffensive all things considered. <br /> <br /> I know that the first chunk of the movie was supposed to be Homura's paradise. But I felt like they just drew it out a bit too long. I can't help but think that I would have liked to see them use some of that time to explore other things, or even just to have another fight in there (considering how awesome Homu vs Mami was, I wouldn't have minded seeing another kickass fight in there). <br /> <br /> It just feels like they could have compressed the first part a bit and used that time to do something I would have enjoyed more. <br /> <br /> A small complaint overall though, I'd rate Madoka Rebellion pretty highly all things considered.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T05:30:57-07:00","id":113983,"title":"","content":"So, new season is out. There's some interesting things so far.<br /> <br /> Anybody watching anything they enjoy?<br /> <br /> I think I'm liking Black Bullet the most so far. It's a lot better than I had thought it would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T10:05:07-07:00","id":129948,"title":"","content":"So! I finally got around to watching the first episode of the Attack on Titan dub. It acquitted itself fairly well.<br /> <br /> .... Right up until that last scene which, for being in my own language (and the quality of the voice acting) actually managed to be more affecting than ever before.<br /> <br /> Sooo, this is looking to be a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T09:19:40-07:00","id":133870,"title":"","content":"I watched Sword Art Online again. I really like the first arc, but still find the Alfheim arc feels like nothing but filler till you get to the end.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Kazuto kind of regresses a bit to me. I mean I get that his obsession blinds him a bit, but it seems pick and choose moments rather than having some believable consistency. I also still can't figure out why he doesn't use two swords at least at important times. Either time he tries to take on the world tree he doesn't bother when it was just shown in the prior fight again that his reaction time is so high he becomes a Cuisinart. Endless mobs would have created the same results, but that would have made me felt he really tried. Espcially the second time he tried it. When I get to that point I just kind of want the anime to be over. Though if they did more I would watch them.<br /> <br /> One other thing is I find the AI child very cheesie, but she has to be my favorite supporting character in spite of that. I still laugh my ass off at her hopping up and down with glee when Kirito is killing mobs. I really don't find much fault with any of the supporting characters save the fact that every other female has to fall for him. Like it wants to almost be a harem anime, but not quite.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know if the manga is out in the us, but I might have to check it out if so. There some definite cliche cheese in there, but I still like the characters and if the personalites between the two are even close it might be a fun read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 05-12-2014, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T17:14:24-07:00","id":134701,"title":"","content":"The OVA hits the harem angle rather hard, with the girls hanging out together and discussing their feelings for Kazuto. I never got all the way through it for that very reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T18:15:08-07:00","id":134731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=133870#post133870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watched Sword Art Online again. I really like the first arc, but still find the Alfheim arc feels like nothing but filler till you get to the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the Alfheim Online game being a really cool setting and a game I'd like to play, the Fairy Dance arc is not only the weakest link in the franchise, it also weakens everything else by its existence.<br /> <br /> I mean, just after freeing everyone from a virtual prison controlled by a GM who might as well be a virtual god, Kirito has to go and do it AGAIN in Alfheim Online? Everyone should have just woken up the first time and put that story to bed.<br /> <br /> If the very next story after SAO was Gun Gale Online, then it wouldn't feel so cheesy that the plot revolves around <i>another </i>game. Among other reasons, because it wouldn't be the third time in a row. Also because the reasons <i>why</i> there's a crisis happening in GGO make sense*, and are better connected to the events of the SAO arc (at least, in the light novels).<br /> <br /> Rather than the Fairy Dance arc, it would have been great if the SAO arc had gotten more content adapted to the screen or outright made for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> * It would have been impossible to trap SAO players in ALO except that both MMOs were being run on the same hardware. I ask you, does it make <i>any</i> sense to burden a game on which peoples <i>lives depend</i> with another, <i>bigger </i>game, bogging down processing power? Or to hook up another full-immersion VRMMO to a game in which people can die, on the off chance that Kayaba might suck them into his trap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-12-2014, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T07:46:03-07:00","id":135353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=134701#post134701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OVA hits the harem angle rather hard, with the girls hanging out together and discussing their feelings for Kazuto. I never got all the way through it for that very reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sucks. I don't mind harem anime, but it really brings down some really great stories by just throwing it in there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=134731#post134731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite the Alfheim Online game being a really cool setting and a game I'd like to play, the Fairy Dance arc is not only the weakest link in the franchise, it also weakens everything else by its existence.<br /> <br /> I mean, just after freeing everyone from a virtual prison controlled by a GM who might as well be a virtual god, Kirito has to go and do it AGAIN in Alfheim Online? Everyone should have just woken up the first time and put that story to bed.<br /> <br /> If the very next story after SAO was Gun Gale Online, then it wouldn't feel so cheesy that the plot revolves around <i>another </i>game. Among other reasons, because it wouldn't be the third time in a row. Also because the reasons <i>why</i> there's a crisis happening in GGO make sense*, and are better connected to the events of the SAO arc (at least, in the light novels).<br /> <br /> Rather than the Fairy Dance arc, it would have been great if the SAO arc had gotten more content adapted to the screen or outright made for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> * It would have been impossible to trap SAO players in ALO except that both MMOs were being run on the same hardware. I ask you, does it make <i>any</i> sense to burden a game on which peoples <i>lives depend</i> with another, <i>bigger </i>game, bogging down processing power? Or to hook up another full-immersion VRMMO to a game in which people can die, on the off chance that Kayaba might suck them into his trap?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was reading that GGO is being made into an anime as well so here is to hoping I like as much as the SAO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T13:41:36-07:00","id":135724,"title":"","content":"If you want to see SAO\u2019s \u201ctrapped in an MMO\u201d genre done right, check out Log Horizon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T13:13:22-07:00","id":137066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=135724#post135724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to see SAO\u2019s \u201ctrapped in an MMO\u201d genre done right, check out Log Horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did enjoy Log Horizon very much. It would have been even better with the kind of budget SAO got. The music, art and fights of Log Horizon are good, but I'd like to have seen them with the kind of quality SAO could put behind fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T14:13:40-07:00","id":137141,"title":"","content":"Anime Network has been showing LH so I've been watching it as they add episodes. So far I like SAO's first arc more for a few reasons. One of which is it just seems a faster pace. Also while it is an over arcing story most episodes are complete in themselves. LH feels like a lazy pace and I don't care for that as much. 5 episodes and not a lot has happened. It feels like it is trying to impress me. Still I'm enjoying it. If nothing else it has the virtue of not being .hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T16:49:36-07:00","id":137350,"title":"","content":"The entire first season is free for streaming on Crunchyroll. I\u2019ll grant that the pace of the series isn\u2019s as fast as in SAO; but paradoxically, that\u2019s because a lot happens in a short period of time in the setting. In SAO, months or years go by between episodes; and the only real changes that occur are either personal (Kirito joins a team that gets slaughtered, etc.) or entirely predictable (the adventurers push on to higher levels). In Log Horizon\u2026 well, I won\u2019t spoil it, other to say that the setting is a much more dynamic one than SAO. That, and it plays with aspects of MMOs that SAO conveniently bypassed, such as the disparity between the player\u2019s appearance and his character\u2019s appearance (disposed of in SAO #1 by the Mirror), the ability to respawn after you\u2019ve been killed (likewise disposed of in SAO #1), the in-game economy (briefly hinted at a few times in SAO, though nothing is ever done with it), and the role of NPCs in the game world (IIRC, there <i>are</i> no NPCs in SAO, save for Kirito\u2019s daughter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:50:21-07:00","id":138221,"title":"","content":"I've heard of Crunchyroll and signed up way in the past, but never really looked at it. Might have to check it out again especially if they are showing for free. I though that was all through their paid stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=137350#post137350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the role of NPCs in the game world (IIRC, there <i>are</i> no NPCs in SAO, save for Kirito\u2019s daughter).</div> </div> </div> </div>It never goes into depth, but it does mention they are there as vendors and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 05-15-2014, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:47:23-07:00","id":138499,"title":"","content":"Crunchyroll\u2019s paid stuff is essentially \u201cview everything ad-free\u201d and \u201cview newly-released stuff\u201d: as a rule of thumb, once an episode has been up for a week you can view it for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T01:42:53-07:00","id":139116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=138499#post138499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crunchyroll\u2019s paid stuff is essentially \u201cview everything ad-free\u201d and \u201cview newly-released stuff\u201d: as a rule of thumb, once an episode has been up for a week you can view it for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also view things with the highest video quality.<br /> <br /> (And a dash of being able to be smug about being the basis for everybody else getting it for free.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T02:56:12-07:00","id":143249,"title":"","content":"I watched the first few episodes of Ghost Hound this weekend; seems promising.<br /> <br /> ...And no wonder, because I just realised that it's written by the Big O guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T08:11:01-07:00","id":143490,"title":"","content":"I have to give thanks for getting me to actually finally check out Crunchyroll. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I watched all of Log Horizon. My opinion of its number two spot to the first arc of SAO didn't really change though I did like it better once it started to get rolling. There were still episodes that seemed slower than they should have been, but that could have just been the nature of the manga as well. Looking forward to season 2.<br /> <br /> Watched Dragon Crisis as well. Meh. I liked the characters, but it was like everything it did was done with half an effort. Everything was done just enough to have the cliche in the anime. Whether it was the action, comedy, harem aspect, etc. I liked it well enough and don't feel my time was wasted with it, but there are many others that have done it much better and I couldn't really see watching it again like I do with some shows.<br /> <br /> I started watching Asura Cryin' so I'll see how that goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T08:14:44-07:00","id":143494,"title":"","content":"Stuff I am watching or read recently:<br /> <br /> Stardust Crusaders anime<br /> <br /> Decoration Disconnection Disorder novel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T08:18:06-07:00","id":167932,"title":"","content":"I finished Pet Girl of Sakurasou.recently and really liked it. Kind of ending that leaves you with warm fuzzies. Started watching Myself; Yourself. So far it is ok. I'm only half way in and it seems like it has had episodes that are nothing but filler. That or it is trying to force the warmth that PGoS fell into more naturally. It seems like it wants to put Sana with Nanaka and Asami as the potential in her way, but even the episodes Nanaka is in she doesn't really feel there. She generally doesn't talk much they just have her standing there in the background all the time. I make her feel more like a part of the background rather than an active participant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T18:59:26-07:00","id":172264,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if there is any good magical girl anime someone could recommend me in which fights push a bit more towards brawling or martial arts rather than mostly throwing around magic projectiles and stuff like that. Bonus points if it could be generally described as lighthearted but not fully comical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T19:46:29-07:00","id":172302,"title":"","content":"It <i>completely</i> misses the boat on being lighthearted; but <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica</i> features magical girls who wield sabres, axes, shields, bows, and muskets \u2014 although Mami\u2019s use of her muskets admittedly borders on throwing around magic projectiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T20:09:17-07:00","id":172318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=172264#post172264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if there is any good magical girl anime someone could recommend me in which fights push a bit more towards brawling or martial arts rather than mostly throwing around magic projectiles and stuff like that. Bonus points if it could be generally described as lighthearted but not fully comical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Futari wa Pretty Cure has a lot of hand to hand combat. I mean sure they typically use their power at the end of the episode to end the fight but mostly martial arts. I can't remember if its Fresh or Suite Pretty Cure but oen of those has loads of hand ot hand as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T20:10:49-07:00","id":172321,"title":"","content":"So I decided to finally start reading Never7. The VN is very well written but I'm having trouble getting into it. I think its mostly because the BGM won't play because of some type of strange read error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T22:20:56-07:00","id":172462,"title":"","content":"Heartcatch Precure had a decent amount of hand to hand figthing - they end the battles by throwing out a big beam, but they usually brawled with the bad guys right up until then.<br /> <br /> Cereal - let me know how it is. I really liked Ever17, but got incredibly bored with Remember11 and ended up dropping it about 1/2 way through the second route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-18-2014, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T06:56:25-07:00","id":172751,"title":"","content":"I finished My Little Monster. It wasn't bad. Something was annoying me about it at first and they it struck me how much like Kare Kano it was, but with an even more comedic take. After that I kept comparing the two the whole time. I think that is why I didn't like it as much as I would have otherwise. Still it wasn't bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}