ll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:01:26-07:00","id":182936,"title":"","content":"I still don't understand all the hype for SnK, it wasn't that great. It was gory, the story wall over the place, loads of angst and what have you. I don't know, maybe I'm just not the target audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:18:10-07:00","id":182968,"title":"","content":"I watched the first episode and had to drop it, not my cup of tea. My girlfriend and my friends, on the other hand, went completly bananas for it (specially her, she watched the first season in just two sits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:21:21-07:00","id":182971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=182936#post182936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't understand all the hype for SnK, it wasn't that great. It was gory, the story wall over the place, loads of angst and what have you. I don't know, maybe I'm just not the target audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've yet ot watch it, but from what I understand it apparently has to do with the characters-apparently they are neat to watch, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T13:26:35-07:00","id":183187,"title":"","content":"Here's a basic summary of my opinion of the merits of Attack on Titan:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attack on Titan is really good at marrying a fantastical premise to a really genuine and human emotional perspective on the ground level, a sliding scale of triumphs and failures in a way that makes for a compelling depiction of an arc that, while ultimately rising, still has occasions where people seem to have all the power in the world or give it everything they've got and yet still fall disastrously short (or possibly an arc that is actually falling into defeat, even though people manage to achieve fist-pumpingly amazing victories), a good pervasive sense of a world ending doom that is still gradual and building up, and manages to be serious, even sometimes dour, without being utterly lifeless or humourless. </div> </div> </div>As an addendum, I'll note my sense that the marriage of human perspective to fantastical premise is that you get all the usual emotional punch of people facing anxiety over broad social and existential fears in general and being in a state of war in particular, while being pitted against an enemy that is viscerally, mortally terrifying and hideous, while also being extremely satisfying to see people take them down. I also feel that part of doing a good job of giving that ground level perspective is that as characters succeed or die, they always get at least some measure of story setup so that even if they're not important, they still feel as though they have enough <i>presence</i> that what happens to them matters. When expanded into the characters who <i>are</i> important... they're not exactly complex (but complexity as a trait of fictional characters is something I feel is overrated anyway), but they're well-developed, reasonably nuanced, and have some fairly strong interpersonal dynamics.<br /> <br /> Also, as a production, it just looks stunning, beautifully animated and detailed, and very well-directed (just some timing and framing alone makes for some amazingly darkly humourous moments), with very distinct character models both for the humans and for the Titans themselves (I feel that having all of the Titans look different plays into just how off-putting they are, even before one gets into how many have such loving detailed grotesquery in the manner of classic European depictions of giants), and the soundtrack is so incredible that it can be enjoyed all on its own (although it really helps to punctuate scenes as they play out).<br /> <br /> All in all, with all of these qualities married together, it managed to evoke genuine emotional reactions from me from the end of the very first episode*, in a way that continuously left me caring significantly about what happened to the characters (such that my internal refrain between episodes 6 and 8 was &quot;don't stop moving, if you stop moving you're dead, keep moving&quot;). And it manages to stay interesting over time by some carefully managed twists and escalations (it's not quite &quot;keep wondering what's going to be pulled out next&quot;, more a sense that as time goes by certain comfortable assumptions start breaking down).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:16:05-07:00","id":183601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=182936#post182936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't understand all the hype for SnK, it wasn't that great. It was gory, the story wall over the place, loads of angst and what have you. I don't know, maybe I'm just not the target audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine anyone who would use &quot;loads of angst&quot; as a criticism, absent of any sort of elaboration, probably isn't.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That was kind of harsh of me, sorry. What I mean is, that, bad stuff happens, and people get upset over it. It's a very angsty show. And, obviously, that's not everybody's cup of tea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":276,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","user":"Merkonan","date":". 06-29-2014, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:52:15-07:00","id":183615,"title":"","content":"I wanted to like SnK - I enjoyed the &quot;survival/horror&quot; aspect of the show, and the way the primary focus was on the human vs titan conflict. Just didn't like the &quot;tweest&quot; that occurred a fourth of the way through the show - it felt like it completely lost the mood and ruined everything I had been enjoying up until then. It might not have been that bad, had the author slowly built up to it and introduced it (much) later on in the series - I just wish the author hadn't &quot;blown his load&quot; so early.<br /> <br /> Oh well. Show's opening was pretty cool anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T01:04:30-07:00","id":183645,"title":"","content":"Did you keep watching after the twist? (not meant as a critique, one way or the other; I\u2019m just curious.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T01:14:18-07:00","id":183648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it felt like it completely lost the mood and ruined everything I had been enjoying up until then.</div> </div> </div> </div> That feeling is incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T03:15:02-07:00","id":183674,"title":"","content":"Eh. If AnubisXy says that a surprise development atroughly the quarter-mark ruined his enjoyment of the series, I\u2019ll take him at his word. I don\u2019t share his experience (if we\u2019re talking about the same surprise, it didn\u2019t ruin my enjoymen in the least \u2014 especially since they <i>didn\u2019t</i> follow up on it in the manner that analogous reveals in other anime tend to be handled. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Erin\u2019s return as a Titan-hating Titan. Traditionally, when the main character gets a \u201cspecial power\u201d like this, everyone else gets relegated to the role of glorified cheering section. Not here: Erin\u2019s unique talent gets recognized by his superiors as a stce; but the actions of his companions and superiors have proven to be <i>every bit as important</i> as anything he has done, before or since. <br /> <br /> As for the pacing of the reveal: you may be making the mistake of thinking that it\u2019s the show\u2019s Big Reveal with insufficient build-up, when in fact it\u2019s merely the first step in the series\u2019 buildup to its big reveal \u2014 which hasn\u2019t come to fruition yet even in the manga.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T04:17:50-07:00","id":183693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If AnubisXy says that a surprise development atroughly the quarter-mark ruined his enjoyment of the series, I\u2019ll take him at his word.</div> </div> </div> </div> If Anubis makes anticipations of developments that are incorrect, I'll correct him. It's about the same as if somebody took the reveal that Darth Vader was Luke Skywalker's father to mean the movies were going to become about a cheerful father-son villain team up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:08:40-07:00","id":183796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=183601#post183601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine anyone who would use &quot;loads of angst&quot; as a criticism, absent of any sort of elaboration, probably isn't.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That was kind of harsh of me, sorry. What I mean is, that, bad stuff happens, and people get upset over it. It's a very angsty show. And, obviously, that's not everybody's cup of tea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> SnKs author said one of his biggest influences was Muv Luv Alternative. I liked the execution of that much better and while they have some similarities but aren't even close to identical I found myself shaking my head at the absurdity of SnK. While its a pretty neat world there are holes in the plot and setting all over. Why didn't the humans just burrow underground and go above at night or whenever the titans aren't active to farm and get their animals seeing as they know they don't mess with livestock and other animals. Why can they develop the technology to fly and have some kind of natural gas to power it but can't develop something that would destroy the titans much easier than cutting the back of their necks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=183615#post183615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to like SnK - I enjoyed the &quot;survival/horror&quot; aspect of the show, and the way the primary focus was on the human vs titan conflict. Just didn't like the &quot;tweest&quot; that occurred a fourth of the way through the show - it felt like it completely lost the mood and ruined everything I had been enjoying up until then. It might not have been that bad, had the author slowly built up to it and introduced it (much) later on in the series - I just wish the author hadn't &quot;blown his load&quot; so early.<br /> <br /> Oh well. Show's opening was pretty cool anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure why it got rid of what I wrote in response to you. I have pretty much the same problem. The twist just took me out of it. I watched until just after the Trost battle. I think part of what made it unappetizing for me was that the twist felt lazy. Instead of having that happen they (the characters) couldn't have gone with an innovative plan? Hell, I would've been okay with the story shifting characters at episode 6 or 7 w/e it was when that happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 06-29-2014, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T11:35:20-07:00","id":183915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=183693#post183693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If Anubis makes anticipations of developments that are incorrect, I'll correct him. It's about the same as if somebody took the reveal that Darth Vader was Luke Skywalker's father to mean the movies were going to become about a cheerful father-son villain team up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anubis just gives out his reason for why he doesn't happen to like something. SnK is obviously a very popular show. So was Breaking Bad. I didn't really enjoy either one all that much, though that doesn't mean I think they were garbage or anything.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It just felt kind of like I had been watching Godzilla, and had been enjoying watching humanityfight Godzilla, and then suddenl+y I was watching King Kong vs Godzilla with the giant monsters duking it out.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm sure that some people, on sitting down to watch Godzilla, and then seeing King Kong show up and deliver a spinning pile-driver to Godzilla would get hella excited, and I might have too if my interest in the series hadn't entirely been on the human element and seeing how they would face off against an unstoppable force of monsters - beating the unstoppable monsters with your own unstoppable monster was very much <i>not</i> what I wanted to see, and I just stopped caring about the show.<br /> <br /> And to be fair, SnK is hardly hardly the first series to introduce plot twists or plot elements that made me stop caring about it and drop it - Bleach, Naruto and Vinland Saga all also immediately spring to mind. SnK just happened to introduce that plot twist very early on.</div></div> </div> </div>-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-29-2014, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:58:16-07:00","id":184063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=183796#post183796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why didn't the humans just burrow underground</div> </div> </div> </div>Because mining habitable spaces is really difficult in terms of logistics and engineering? Also probably wouldn't really keep the Titans out; the walls work because they're too thick to break through and too tall to climb; getting something with the same kind of integrity for underground would be more difficult, I imagine; you'd get 15-metre classes digging and tearing their way through and 3 to 5-metre classes getting into the holes. Come to think of it, you'd mostly have Titans constantly crowded around the entrances to such habitations (much as they crowd around the wall gates) and they're not so sessile at night that people right next to them while unrestrained would get through unscathed. The gates can at least be cleared when expeditions need to head out because of the advantage of higher ground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">go above at night or whenever the titans aren't active to farm and get their animals seeing as they know they don't mess with livestock and other animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think farming at night would be very effective, considering how photosynthesis works. Livestock also seems fairly likely to wander off if left unsupervised for half the day (or scared off by the giant monsters), and not really effectively managed while sleeping. And even if people are away from those places during the day, I imagine they still attract Titans just from the scent of them, and that would be likely to lead to them being trampled.<br /> <br /> Yes, the image of some intrepid farmed adventurer returning to their secret crops and livestock enclosures at night only to find that they've all been crushed seems quite suitable to the usual milieu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can they develop the technology to fly and have some kind of natural gas to power it but can't develop something that would destroy the titans much easier than cutting the back of their necks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really call 3D Maneuver Gear flight, and even then that doesn't really matter, since technological progression doesn't work that way, and even if it did, the way Titans are set up makes me feel like there aren't that many ways that would be more effective.<br /> <br /> These aren't plot holes, by the way, they're just nitpicking, of the kind that no setting can stand up to simply because any reasonably intelligent person can find a way to logically propose how anything in a fictional world can be other than how it is. Neither can real life, for that matter, anything from international responses to the growth of the Nazi movement to the very fact that life exists at all (something so chemically and mathematically improbable that it actually creates a credible basis for the idea of alien progenitors, even if that's only really pushing event zero back a bit).<br /> <br /> Minor spoiler for the general tone of the series as a whole:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Still and all, between what happens in the show and some vague things I've gathered from information about the progression in the manga that I'm otherwise deliberately ignorant of, there's a gradual implication that there's something sinister behind the social system underlying the series.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of what made it unappetizing for me was that the twist felt lazy. Instead of having that happen they (the characters) couldn't have gone with an innovative plan? Hell, I would've been okay with the story shifting characters at episode 6 or 7 w/e it was when that happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was what they did in the supply depot not innovative? Or the full details of how they ended the battle? Dataweaver is right, it's not as if all other characters become props and spectators from there on in.<br /> <br /> Spoiler for episode 7 onwards, related to previous spoiler:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's not as if Eren's transformation constitutes much of an instant win button either, considering that he can barely control or understand it, and everybody around him is really damn testy about how much he uses it; as far as I've seen in the series, people seem continuously on edge as to whether each time Eren transforms will be the time where they lose him completely.<br /> <br /> It also contributes to the tone of the series because <i>nobody has a clue how he's able to do that</i>, and it throws all kinds of assumptions into confusion and doubt, especially as certain things unfold in the story. The revelation of Eren's transformation is an asset, but it's mostly a disturbing mystery.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> People have compared Attack on Titan to a zombie story, and while I don't quite think it's the best thing to try and sell people on the series with, one basic tenet carries through; zombies are freaky in a manner that contributes to tone, but they're not really interesting antagonists, or even really antagonists at all, they're a force that binds people into situations that bring social complications to the forefront, and occasionally something of unknown and uncanny nature and origins that need to be unraveled. The manner of the so-called twist is part of playing into the premise of just how powerful the Titan are, but it doesn't really redirect the focus or tone of the series, because if the series was just about fighting the giant monsters it wouldn't be nearly as interesting.<br /> <br /> As for being foreshadowed, what did one think that those injections were about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T17:12:28-07:00","id":184221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184063#post184063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think farming at night would be very effective, considering how photosynthesis works. Livestock also seems fairly likely to wander off if left unsupervised for half the day (or scared off by the giant monsters), and not really effectively managed while sleeping. And even if people are away from those places during the day, I imagine they still attract Titans just from the scent of them, and that would be likely to lead to them being trampled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crops run on a cycle long enough to the point that they don't care much about when the seed is in the ground or when the plants are harvested. The problem is that at night you'd need a lot of light to see what you're doing. If you're doing it by hand, planting weeding, harvesting all need light, and if you're scaling up to where you're feeding a lot of people and mechanizing it, you've now got need for a lot of area to be lit up so you can work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T18:58:42-07:00","id":184314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184063#post184063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Still and all, between what happens in the show and some vague things I've gathered from information about the progression in the manga that I'm otherwise deliberately ignorant of, there's a gradual implication that there's something sinister behind the social system underlying the series.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There\u2019s more going on in the series than \u201cgiant humaniod monsters go on a rampage\u201d; and in fact the Titanic rampage is merely a symptom of the <i>real</i> problem. The series has, from the very beginning, asked the question \u201cjust where did the Titans come from in the first place?\u201d \u2014 and Ehren\u2019s transformation is a vital piece to the puzzle, without which humans would continue stumbling around blindly.</div></div> </div> </div> If you don\u2019t like the twist or what the story is <i>actually</i> about, so be it; not every anime is for everyone. But the premise <i>isn\u2019t</i> poorly thought out, nor is the twist a cheat. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184063#post184063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was what they did in the supply depot not innovative? Or the full details of how they ended the battle? Dataweaver is right, it's not as if all other characters become props and spectators from there on in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Far from it. Traditionally, when something like SnK\u2019s twist takes place in an anime, the Ehren counterpart starts calling the shots. In SnK, Ehren has not displayed any sort of leadership, tactical, or even unusual fighting prowess; and he\u2019s very ignorant of what\u2019s going on. Others with more competence in these areas continue to take center stage where these things matter; and Ehren only takes the spotlight when brute force is called for \u2014 which is surprisingly rare, considering the brutality of the Titans. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184063#post184063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for being foreshadowed, what did one think that those injections were about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Frankly, I\u2019m not sure what more they could have done in terms of foreshadowing, given that the whole point of the reveal was that nobody involved knew that such a thing was possible. As I implied before, the reason why the reveal came so early was precisely <i>because</i> it\u2019s not the \u201cbig secret\u201d of the series: it\u2019s merely an early indicator that \u201chumanity vs. giant zombies\u201d is an oversimplification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T22:08:18-07:00","id":184538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184063#post184063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The manner of the so-called twist is part of playing into the premise of just how powerful the Titan are, but it doesn't really redirect the focus or tone of the series, because if the series was just about fighting the giant monsters it wouldn't be nearly as interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you know, that's just like, your opinion, man.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">More seriously, I'm a fan of zombie movies. And I enjoyed 28 Days Later well enough.<br /> <br /> But if the movie had instead been a television show, and a quarter of the way through, the MC had turned into super-zombie-man, I'd have probably lost interest in it, and dropped it like I did SnK, as I would have preferred it if they had kept to the original premise of &quot;humans vs zombies&quot; (or &quot;humans vs giant zombies&quot; in the case of SnK)</div></div> </div> </div>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-30-2014, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T23:30:31-07:00","id":184565,"title":"","content":"Not that I didn't know that was coming, because seriously I live on the internet(I am in your servers, I am <i>in your mind</i>), but, uh, Anubis, spoilers for anyone else? Your description is a little spot on for people who actually care about spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T02:26:49-07:00","id":184675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184538#post184538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you know, that's just like, your opinion, man.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> But if the movie had instead been a television show, and a quarter of the way through, the MC had turned into super-zombie-man)</div></div> </div> </div>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Turning into a super zombie man is ridiculously excessive for something that is no bigger than and not much stronger than a regular human. That doesn't mean that no zombie story ever had that one badass who manages to mow zombies down. Eren is... not quite that, for the aforementioned reason that his transformaton is barely under control.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it would have taken all of one more episode to disabuse you of your misconception.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T03:34:46-07:00","id":184712,"title":"","content":"I feel I've devised a more apt comparison: It's akin to liking Batman Begins right up until that costumed ninja fellow pops up, and not even managing to see the premise for the sequel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T09:14:23-07:00","id":184880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184712#post184712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel I've devised a more apt comparison: It's akin to liking Batman Begins right up until that costumed ninja fellow pops up, and not even managing to see the premise for the sequel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really that bizarre to believe that someone dislikes a show you like?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T09:25:19-07:00","id":184889,"title":"","content":"It's the anime subculture's way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T11:37:56-07:00","id":184970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184880#post184880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it really that bizarre to believe that someone dislikes a show you like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think his main objection is that the stated reason for not liking the show strikes Isator Levi as Missing The Point. <br /> <br /> But yeah; I have no objection to you not liking something I like, or vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T11:46:15-07:00","id":184974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it really that bizarre to believe that someone dislikes a show you like?</div> </div> </div> </div> If it was, I'd have called it akin to watching Batman Begins and deciding that it wasn't to their tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T12:29:12-07:00","id":184993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=183645#post183645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you keep watching after the twist? (not meant as a critique, one way or the other; I\u2019m just curious.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Missed the post.<br /> <br /> \u200bI watched a couple more episodes, where they were moving the rock. I really wasn't enjoying the direction of the show, so I got online, looked through some spoilers about what would happen next, and decided I just wasn't much interested anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=184712#post184712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel I've devised a more apt comparison: It's akin to liking Batman Begins right up until that costumed ninja fellow pops up, and not even managing to see the premise for the sequel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gee, condescending much?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">More like it's going to the new Godzilla movie, watching Godzilla smash up the city, wonder how in the hell people are going to fight Godzilla and then see the main character turn into King Kong. <br /> <br /> Some people might enjoy that. Lots of people might enjoy it. But other people, might not really care for it much at all.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean, to be clear my view is probably in the minority. SnK is hugely popular. It was the best selling manga this last quarter, outselling One Piece (which has been the previous best selling manga every quarter for the last three years) by several million volume.<br /> <br /> I just wanted the show to be one thing, and it ended up as something else. That's not the show's fault. I don't really think it's my fault much either. Who knows, I'll keep myself apprised of spoilers and such, and if the series ever ends up doing things I'm more interested in, I might pick it up. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So far though, King Kong... I mean, Beast Titan, definitely ain't doing it for me.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T12:32:41-07:00","id":184996,"title":"","content":"Of course really looking forward to a second season of SAO as long as it plays more like the first arc than the second. Log Horizon got better toward the end if it comes out of the gate with that pacing it will be fine. I fear though it will go back to feeling like it is slogging along and I'll loose interest quick.<br /> <br /> I like Attack on Titan for the most part. I didn't mind the reveal(something had to happen since everything else make him seem a fuck up),but felt that it wasn't really used well. I feel like all of the characters have a too short attention span because they always seem to be forgetting important pieces of what is going on until it is too inconvenient or impossible for them to do anything about it. And I'm put off by how often the characters are made blatantly stupid for dramatic tension.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The penultimate of that is the forest plot and his whole group getting wiped out because the whole &quot;trust us/believe in us&quot; thing. That was utterly fucking stupid. Its a tie for me if the first or second fight with the female titan is the stupidest moment.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also hate how little growth there is on all of them, but especially Eren. It seems like the moment he shows any hit of being better at anything the rung is pulled out from under him. I'm so tried of the heroes that magically fuck up into winning every situation they are allowed to win instead of actually gradually becoming better.<br /> <br /> Still I like the characters(that are still around) enough and at least I'm not left with a sense that every living thing is dying because the writer likes pinning bugs to a cork board or tearing wings off flies(in spite of some pointless deaths), so I'm game for a second season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T15:25:08-07:00","id":185158,"title":"","content":"Really, to answer the question of what makes Attack on Titan stand out, what makes it more than the gore and the angst, and what makes the twist fail to undermine the tone of the series is because it's not about gore and angst, nor about fighting Titans. Hell, it's not even about the mysteries.<br /> <br /> It's children huddled in a refugee camp struggling for food before their families are sent out to die to relieve resource shortages (and then joining the military in order to still have access to food). It's huddling in fear, shaking, praying and cursing before being sent out into battle. It's corruption and division and people putting themselves through the wronger and climbing over the others just so that they can get one level further in. It's the note that, if the second wall is breached, then hiding behind the last one won't matter, because it can't provide the food for anybody.<br /> <br /> But it's also a young girl being assured that the world hasn't ended despite losing everything by having a scarf wrapped around her head. Of facing something overwhelming and unstoppable with nothing but fierce determination out of the determination to live for the sake of a loved one's memory. It's a throng of terrified rabble holding together in the face of Hell when they're told that falling apart will leave their families exposed to that Hell. Of people throwing themselves into the fray just to create an opening that their one, slim hope can get through at the cost of their own lives, and leaping into the literal jaws of death in order to drag a comrade out even to take their place. And it's a young man who only ever wanted to be exemplary so that he could escape to a life of ease taking up the greatest danger and difficulty in the world because to do anything else would disgrace the memory of a friend.<br /> <br /> It's a setting, a scenario, and a cast of characters who are in every way worthy of those words in my signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T08:46:23-07:00","id":188754,"title":"","content":"So Sailor Moon Crystal episode 1 was immensely satisfying to me, although the animation on the transformation sequence is a little weird(and why do we get a close up ass shot?). A lot of good story framing devices were used here, and I'm kinda glad they're not even hiding certain aspects. Can't wait for Ami next week!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:54:57-07:00","id":188787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=188754#post188754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Sailor Moon Crystal episode 1 was immensely satisfying to me, although the animation on the transformation sequence is a little weird(and why do we get a close up ass shot?). A lot of good story framing devices were used here, and I'm kinda glad they're not even hiding certain aspects. Can't wait for Ami next week!</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, good! I won't get to watch it until this evening, but I'm happy to hear its good. I was a little worried, because the animation has some very weird quirks, like the 3D transformation sequence and what my partner calls &quot;O face&quot;. Your words reassure me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T10:27:10-07:00","id":188799,"title":"","content":"The art style of the show actually works really well in motion-all my old concerns about it being a little to stock-still was neatly removed today.<br /> <br /> I suppose, as one reviewer pointed out, this means we're going to have less humor animation(Chibi's/Slapstick art/etc.) but considering the manga had less of that to begin with anyways, that's okie dokey lokie for me.<br /> <br /> THe attitude towards certain secrets of the series is also, admittedly, hit or miss-I kind of like the fact they don't bother since fans know, but I can see some people being annoyed that it becomes even more apparent. I suppose one incident in particular(you'll know it) does make Usagi more of an idiot, but small prices.<br /> <br /> Still. this was a <i>fantastic</i> start to the series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T12:40:39-07:00","id":188876,"title":"","content":"The first episode of SAOII was a lot more talk-heavy than I expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T08:12:00-07:00","id":190304,"title":"","content":"Sooo, anyone catch Knights of Sidonia? Pretty entertaining play on a mecha show, and definitely looks like it would be great inspiration for a Gunstar Campaign. Hmmm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T10:44:25-07:00","id":190476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=190304#post190304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo, anyone catch Knights of Sidonia? Pretty entertaining play on a mecha show, and definitely looks like it would be great inspiration for a Gunstar Campaign. Hmmm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind spoilers so I spoiled it and decided it wasn't for me. I'm a generally negative person so I like shows that leave me positive and not just reinforce that negativity. I'm not saying the situations I read would do that for everyone, but that was my take away from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T12:37:09-07:00","id":190623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=190304#post190304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo, anyone catch Knights of Sidonia? Pretty entertaining play on a mecha show, and definitely looks like it would be great inspiration for a Gunstar Campaign. Hmmm?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been following the manga for awhile now. It's by Nihei, the same fellow who did Blame! (one of my all time favorite series). Knights of Sidionia is rather fun with some surprising twists. The anime was a very good adaptation, with a few changes or alterations here or there (for the better for the most part). The one issue I have with it is that it's CG. I don't necessarily dislike CG shows, but in this case, I felt that doing it in CG ruins a lot of the atmosphere. <br /> <br /> In the manga, Sidonia itself has as much personality as any of the characters, thanks to Nihei's artstyle. He manages to make the place look ancient; it's supposed to have been flying around for hundreds of years. With the CG however, everything looks too crisp and too new. So you lose the sense that humanity is living in this ancient, rusting hulk. It's not a huge problem, but I found myself pining for Nihei's artstyle. I think the animation staff acknowledged this as well; during the commercial breaks they'd have pages from the manga showing off Sidonia's scenery.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, it had my favorite opening song in years. I really loved the way they took the oath of the Knights of Sidonia and turned it into the lyrics for the song.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T12:24:43-07:00","id":195657,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine has been bugging me to watch Fairy Tail. However, these days I a series has to be really good for me to go for 40+ episodes and I know this one has at least 150, so I'd like to hear some opinions about it. Is it worth the hype? And is there much filler in it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T12:54:17-07:00","id":195669,"title":"","content":"Well, it's your average shounen, not a brilliant piece of animu art, but if you are bored and have too much of spare time, like fanservice shoved around and won't think much about it making sense, sure why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T20:00:18-07:00","id":195958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=195657#post195657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine has been bugging me to watch Fairy Tail. However, these days I a series has to be really good for me to go for 40+ episodes and I know this one has at least 150, so I'd like to hear some opinions about it. Is it worth the hype? And is there much filler in it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fairy Tail is pretty much the stereotypical example of a standard shounen. The fights are all solved with the power of friendship and there's a lot of fanservice.<br /> <br /> That said, it does it excel with the characters. The series has a lot of characters and they're all very cool. Erza is probably one of the coolest and most badass female characters in any series.<br /> <br /> As far as shounen series go, I'd rate Fairy Tail a solid 7/10. It's not bad, but outside of the characters it's not all that great. If you're thinking of trying out a long-running shounen series, I'd recommend One Piece. It's superior in just about every way (and if you do, just stick to the anime).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-13-2014, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T01:50:57-07:00","id":196137,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'll pass on Fairy Tail, then. If it was, say, less than 30 episodes I might give it a go, but since it is 5 times that (or more?), no chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T04:56:27-07:00","id":196193,"title":"","content":"I would recommend Tatami Galaxy since though I'm yet to watch it, people I know consistently tell me it's a good comedy, and it's short enough for your preferences (13 or so, I think).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:56:37-07:00","id":196377,"title":"","content":"what kind of show are you looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T12:55:06-07:00","id":196528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=196193#post196193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would recommend Tatami Galaxy since though I'm yet to watch it, people I know consistently tell me it's a good comedy, and it's short enough for your preferences (13 or so, I think).</div> </div> </div> </div>Tatami Galaxy is really, really good and I would recommend anyone watch it, but while it has comedy elements, you probably shouldn't go into it expecting a comedy, at least not like your typical comedy anime.<br /> <br /> If I don't know what sort of series someone might prefer, but they're looking for something that's fairly short, is good and doesn't have any glaring flaws, I normally recommend Angel Beats. It has action, comedy, romance, drama, mystery... just about everything, and it manages to do all of it pretty well. Just make sure you don't wiki it or spoil yourself. It's only 13 episodes (that's like 5 hours). Go into it blind. You definitely won't regret watching it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-13-2014, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T16:08:36-07:00","id":196600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=196377#post196377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what kind of show are you looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually not actively looking for anything, but since I'm running out of episodes for a few of the things I have been watching, I wouldn't mind recommendations within the following guidelines:<ul><li><b>Combat</b>: I'm in the mood for fighting animes. It doesn't have to be overly violent or necessarily the major focus. I also have a distinct preference for melee and hand to hand fighting or combined melee and ranged fighting over a major focus on firearms or just throwing magic at opponents or things like that.</li> <li><b>Non-Ecchi: </b>little to no fanservice is a preference. Alternatively, equal-opportunity fanservice also works for me. Fanservice that is well justified within a good narrative is also okay (like, a sexy scene because one character is trying to seduce another is probably OK. All the female characters coincidentally having their clothes sexily destroyed in battle is probably not, though I do excuse a lot if it is played for comedy)</li> <li><b>Non-Tragedy</b>: I don't mind a serious plot, though I'm slightly more in the mood for something lighthearted lately. Definitively nothing too dramatic and absolutely no tragedies, though.</li> <li><b>Short</b>: something with less than 30 episodes is preferable, but it is not that big of a deal up to 40-50. Only something really good to get me to watch 60+ episodes and truly phenomenal for 100+</li> <li><b>Animation/Artwork</b>: I'm an art guy, so it is hard for me to overlook poor animation and artwork even if the story is good</li> <li><b>Not exceedingly shonen</b>: I don't mind shonen anime, but I prefer ones that don't rely too heavily on the tropes of the genre.</li> </ul><br /> Stuff I have on my list to watch or re-watch include stuff like: both seasons of Ghost in the Shell: Stand Alone Complex plus the Solid State Society movie, Heartcatch Precure (and probably other Precure after I finish it, since I really liked it), Big O, possibly Durarara! (I have only seen 3 episodes, so I'm not sure if it is my cup of tea), Birdy the Mighty: Decode.<br /> <br /> And among the Mangas/Manhuas/Webtoons: The Gamer, Tower of God, Onepunch-Man, The Breaker: New Waves (already read The Breaker), Noblesse, Ability, History's Strongest Disciple Kenichi (I like the premise, but it is <b>so </b>shonen it hurts and the fanservice has grown to ridiculous levels over time, so I'm currently giving it a break), Vagabond, Teppuu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T18:27:32-07:00","id":196626,"title":"","content":"combat but non tragedy with little to no fanservice. Have you seen Girls und Panzer yet? Not exactly combat but its about highschool girls driving tanks<br /> <br /> Check out Bartender. There is no combat. there is no fanservice. Its maybe 13 episodes. I don't know how to describe except as the most relaxing anime I've ever watched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 07-13-2014, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T00:35:30-07:00","id":196655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=196600#post196600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually not actively looking for anything, but since I'm running out of episodes for a few of the things I have been watching, I wouldn't mind recommendations within the following guidelines:</div> </div> </div> </div>Baccano! if you haven't seen it yet. It fits your criteria and is damn good. Also, it's by the same guy who wrote Durarara, but I think it's quite a bit better. There's a couple of characters from Baccano who briefly show up in Durarara, nothing major, but it's a cool moment, so you might as well watch it first if you're planning to watch Durarara; it's also shorter than Durarara..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T11:51:42-07:00","id":197064,"title":"","content":"On Fariy Tale I had made it through the first 50 a while back on Netflix. Now that I'm using Crunchyroll I decided just recently to try the next....100+??? I got two in and quit. I still like the characters but there is just way too much filler like so many of these series have. I can't see going through that many more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T08:38:00-07:00","id":202166,"title":"","content":"So the next episodeof Sailor Moon Crystal came out, and now I have a few gripes. It's been a while since I read the manga, so this isn't really a whole on comparison.<br /> <br /> 1)What's with the dialogue? So much of it seems really weird, particularly for Ami, having her say things that seem really out of place for her character(describing Luna as an angel who came out of the sky when she clearly jumped out of a tree? what?). Some of it is stupid, and some of it is out of character(even if the afore mentioned scene wasn't stupid, Ami doesn't describe things like that).<br /> 2)So Mamoru being in a tux in the first episode was cute, even cheeky, and somewhat justified given the event. But for him to be running around in that tux <i>all the damn time</i>? That's not funny, that's lazy guys.<br /> 3)I can't remember if the manga did this or not, but I feel like we got a clear understanding who the enemy is by now. But as is, I don't think our heroes even know who they're fighting or why, beyond quick little snippets that don't stick.<br /> 4)I've often described the Sailor Moon manga as being surprisingly WoD-esque. This episode was a great example....that somehow lost that in translation.<br /> <br /> Still, despite this, and some other weird choices(why is that ridge over Sailor Moon's ass in the transformation sequence, seriously?), TOday was still a fun episode that introduces Best Sailor Ami Mizuno(giving her glasses definitely made her cuter, which I guess speaks to my fetishes), and despite my desire to see them mix the original anime episode and the manga chapter together, it was still a thrill to see that variation of the story come to life. And now that we have Best Scout, things can only get better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T15:09:13-07:00","id":203269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</