Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T22:46:45-07:00","id":280628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=215887#post215887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finished Maoyu last night on Crunchyroll. That was really great. Would have liked a little more fighting put in there some where, but over all really enjoyed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you enjoyed Maoyu I'd check out Spice and Wolf and/or Log Horizon. Log Horizon is supposed to be based on a set of novels by the same author as Maoyu. It is a similar take on the people trapped in Sword Art Online storyline, with differences. Among those is the fact that they seem to be literally in an entire other world that is similar to the MMO they were playing when they got sucked in. Also, they were not playing Virtual Reality, they were playing a standard MMO and suddenly pop...other world.<br /> <br /> Log Horizon focuses a lot on politics and the ramifications you would have in trying to rein in a bunch of nigh-immortal types.<br /> <br /> Since I mentioned Sword Art Online, I am going to discuss Sword Art Online II<br /> <br /> I have a friend who thinks people should stop watching after they finish the Aincrad storyline and escape the first game. I don't agree, I like the Alfheim Online storyline just as much. I had heard of the later storylines from the wiki and had been eager to see them get their own series, however, I'm slightly disappointing in SAO II.<br /> <br /> It took too long to build up. Almost none of the fight scenes held near the emotional impact or excellent choreography held by the major fights in the first series. The philosophical theme it held at its heart (warrior's guilt essentially) was handled simultaneously with anvils and shallow water. Kirito's keen insights that he used to such great effect in SAO were fairly well dumbed down until they finally had him have an epiphany and outline the entire villainous plot near the end of the sequence (I'm not doubting he could do that, I'm just not seeing this murder mystery as being anywhere near as difficult as the one he solved in SAO).<br /> <br /> Granted some of this is likely that the SAO series was a story stretched out over something like two years of world time with an extra two or three days for the Alfheim Online story....and SAOII covers about two to four days of action. In that regard, Kirito solved the Death Gun issue as quickly as he solved the mystery of the duel-less deaths in the town zone, but stretching out his investigation over 13 episodes made it seem like he had gone from brilliant detective to dullard. Someone could point out that the same could be said of the situation in the Alfheim arc, but at least there we were given several awesome fight scenes to fill in the gap. SAOII focused on the investigation for most of 13 episodes and settled for exposition to have Kirito get used to the new game rather than throwing him into situations such as the politics of war in ALO or the ambushes or so on.<br /> <br /> There was also an overuse of Kirito's berserker fighting style. Everytime he had a fight in SAOII we were shown him going aggressive on the level to his desperation against Gleam Eyes or the army blocking the way up the World Tree. While Kirito's normal fighting style is high speed and extremely aggressive, he does not slip into berserk with every fight in either half of SAO. But it seems like his discipline and self-control have devolved in the time since solving the ALO crisis, because the animators seemed to feel the need to give us wild eyes and berserking on all his fights against the gunners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T02:51:25-07:00","id":280763,"title":"","content":"I know Arc likes UBW anime so far. What is the opinion of others here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:35:15-07:00","id":281037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=280539#post280539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You assumed that everyone knew what AMV Hell was; I didn\u2019t even know what AMV stood for, let alone anything about AMV Hell, so I was asking for clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>AMVHell is particularly... brain stressing?<br /> <br /> Watching them is kinda like watching a contest where the entries have to be 5-30 second audio clips set to anime video clips with the intention of disturbing the viewer as much as possible. And then you watch several dozen of them.<br /> <br /> It's fun, but you also end up with a lot of song clips stuck in your head and a lot of anime that you go &quot;what is that from?&quot; and usually a small pile of new shows to watch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:25:23-07:00","id":281135,"title":"","content":"I'm making Changeling character, either as GMPC, PC or NPC, and she's Fairest/Lionhearted (the latter is a homebrew Kith from 1d4chan). After discussing it with my friend I went full Fate/Apocrypha weeb and here is the faceclaim (mixing Mask and Mien)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/EUck1eW.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> All glory to Changeling!Mo(e)rdred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to 