ute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-15-2014, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T22:37:16-07:00","id":283403,"title":"","content":"Mordred ? I always thought her/his dominant color being red for some reason.<br /> <br /> And didn't TM announce a Tsukihime remake a while back ? I do hope Akiha's power get more detail and explanation this time since it's the thing the make me really interested in TM back then, I mean, she is sucking the heat out of your body using invisible magic red hair !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T09:59:42-07:00","id":283933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=280628#post280628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you enjoyed Maoyu I'd check out Spice and Wolf and/or Log Horizon. Log Horizon is supposed to be based on a set of novels by the same author as Maoyu. It is a similar take on the people trapped in Sword Art Online storyline, with differences. Among those is the fact that they seem to be literally in an entire other world that is similar to the MMO they were playing when they got sucked in. Also, they were not playing Virtual Reality, they were playing a standard MMO and suddenly pop...other world.<br /> <br /> Log Horizon focuses a lot on politics and the ramifications you would have in trying to rein in a bunch of nigh-immortal types.</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched LH and liked it. Not quite as much as SAO, but enjoyed it. I know it is only 2/3 episodes so far, but I was hoping for LH2 to come right out of the box running with how LH1 ended and it more kind of hiccuped. I'm sure that is more my impatiences talking than the anime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since I mentioned Sword Art Online, I am going to discuss Sword Art Online II<br /> <br /> I have a friend who thinks people should stop watching after they finish the Aincrad storyline and escape the first game. I don't agree, I like the Alfheim Online storyline just as much. I had heard of the later storylines from the wiki and had been eager to see them get their own series, however, I'm slightly disappointing in SAO II.<br /> <br /> It took too long to build up. Almost none of the fight scenes held near the emotional impact or excellent choreography held by the major fights in the first series. The philosophical theme it held at its heart (warrior's guilt essentially) was handled simultaneously with anvils and shallow water. Kirito's keen insights that he used to such great effect in SAO were fairly well dumbed down until they finally had him have an epiphany and outline the entire villainous plot near the end of the sequence (I'm not doubting he could do that, I'm just not seeing this murder mystery as being anywhere near as difficult as the one he solved in SAO).<br /> <br /> Granted some of this is likely that the SAO series was a story stretched out over something like two years of world time with an extra two or three days for the Alfheim Online story....and SAOII covers about two to four days of action. In that regard, Kirito solved the Death Gun issue as quickly as he solved the mystery of the duel-less deaths in the town zone, but stretching out his investigation over 13 episodes made it seem like he had gone from brilliant detective to dullard. Someone could point out that the same could be said of the situation in the Alfheim arc, but at least there we were given several awesome fight scenes to fill in the gap. SAOII focused on the investigation for most of 13 episodes and settled for exposition to have Kirito get used to the new game rather than throwing him into situations such as the politics of war in ALO or the ambushes or so on.<br /> <br /> There was also an overuse of Kirito's berserker fighting style. Everytime he had a fight in SAOII we were shown him going aggressive on the level to his desperation against Gleam Eyes or the army blocking the way up the World Tree. While Kirito's normal fighting style is high speed and extremely aggressive, he does not slip into berserk with every fight in either half of SAO. But it seems like his discipline and self-control have devolved in the time since solving the ALO crisis, because the animators seemed to feel the need to give us wild eyes and berserking on all his fights against the gunners. </div> </div> </div>I think SAO is my favorite stuck in MMO story by far. I really didn't like AFO storyline(anmie haven't read the manga) because it really didn't seem to get what made SAO good. I like SAO2 better than AFO, but not as much as the first arch of SAO. I agree the build up took too long and they wasted 2 1/2 episodes on recap.<br /> <br /> I admit I was also disappointed in Kirito as a character a bit. I can understand that he might have had issues with what he did, but it did seem a little too self loathing for him at first. As you say he has always had quick insights and this time he didn't really show any of that till the very end. The other thing off was outside of those &quot;I'm a killer moments&quot; he was totally fine. I would have found it more believable if he had already seemed to have faced it and got over it during SAO itself. He kind of showed that between what he did in SAO and how he ended it with<br /> <br /> I agree the combat was often lacking. I did love those Ninja Jedi moments though. Totally geeked out. I was disappointed in his fight with Death Gun. It seemed a big step back compared to the fighter he was in SAO and they re-showed in the beginning. I agree it felt stretched out, but that didn't seem to be his issue but all the filler in between. Didn't really see the berserk you did. He seemed quick and in control to me for most of his fight. Might have to watch it again. DG fight was the only one I was disappointed in. Otherwise I just wanted more.<br /> <br /> We have more season two coming so here is hoping. I don't remember what came after GGO. I'll have to look up the Wiki again. Oh and I'm hoping for more Asuna(I really liked the chemistry they created between the two characters in SAO and the comedy that came from it), but as far as I remember reading about she doesn't really factor much in most of the arcs going forward. There and important to Kirito, but no real presence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:28:30-07:00","id":284140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mordred ? I always thought her/his dominant color being red for some reason.<br /> <br /> And didn't TM announce a Tsukihime remake a while back ? I do hope Akiha's power get more detail and explanation this time since it's the thing the make me really interested in TM back then, I mean, she is sucking the heat out of your body using invisible magic red hair ! </div> </div> </div>Funny you mention her/his, since originally they thought about making Mordred a guy that just looks so girly, but when Mordred was about get full characterization in Apocrypha, Higashide and Nasu changed it since as she is a clone it would not make sense and they had no room for two girly looking guys (Astolfo is possibly girlier than any female character in Nasuverse).<br /> <br /> She is sucking life force to be more precise, heat being interchangeable with that. There was a mention that fully inverted Akiha (Kohaku route Akiha close to that) could go against Servants because of her powers being good at draining them from prana. But she would be batshit insane beyond recovery, most likely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T17:41:27-07:00","id":284378,"title":"","content":"The original F/SN and Tsuikihime seem to lean heavily on prior knowledge of the minutiae from the visual novels. Fate/Zero is much better for introducing new people to the metaphysics and history. But starting with that spoils stuff in F/SN. I'm waiting for the new HF track to get on Hulu so I can watch it. (Yes, I live in Japan. No I don't have a TV)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T13:35:01-07:00","id":285264,"title":"","content":"Seriously, read Tsukihime VN but with Tsukihime Anime OST (just drop tracks on your own, you can edit OST through drag and copy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. M