ank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T12:04:43-08:00","id":309362,"title":"","content":"Another Fate/Extra game after CCC announced, apparently.<br /> <br /> I only wish Nero gets axed, since she is ridiculous. <br /> <br /> I would prefer Lancer, Rider and Assassin this time as playable classes, but if we get same classes as before, I want male Saber class Servant this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T21:45:42-08:00","id":309860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=309362#post309362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Fate/Extra game after CCC announced, apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Nasu writing it? He said Fate/Extra CCC was his &quot;magnum opus&quot; for the Fate series and he probably wasn't going to write any other major stories for Fate. But you know how writers often change their minds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T22:05:20-08:00","id":309865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=308326#post308326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't expecting fast paced, I've been really disappointed in Log Horizon so far. I really hope it picks up a bit. Doesn't have to be action, just actually move forward in a meaningful way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you are in the series. Personally I'm digging on Log Horizon, though I understand if it's not everyone's cup of tea. Kind of slow paced with lots of world building, politics, economics and round table-type discussions. Also some people really didn't likethe &quot;introduction to MMOs episode&quot; where the new players learn how to party, but I think it should be mandatory watching before anyone plays an MMO (&quot;wait for the tank to get aggro and get out of the fire guy's!&quot;)<br /> <br /> I wasn't as big of a fan of SOA - it just didn't feel as MMO's, probably because it didn't really use any mechanics and Kirito was able to basically solo his way through everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:56:06-08:00","id":310577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=308522#post308522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve been quite happy with Log Horizon thus far. It <i>has</i> been moving forward in meaningful ways; it\u2019s just been somewhat understated about them: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">in particular, we\u2019re starting to see some unintended consequences of the \u201cworld-class spell\u201d that turned a Person of the Land into an Adventurer, blurring the line between the two: for instance, flavor text of all sorts is starting to become real, a fact that Krusty is not too happy about.</div></div> </div> </div>Of course, I also tend to appreciate shows that lay solid groundwork for a future payoff.<br /> <br /> And am I the only one who finds it disconcerting that SAO hasn\u2019t actually had any SAO in it since the middle of the first season? I mean, the hundred-level dungeon has been integrated into Alfheim Online as its world tree; but it\u2019s being explored by fairies, not by swordsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is the establishing of some of those things were done in a couple minutes out of the 144(guesstamite 24*6) minutes so far. I wasn't expecting a lot in the first episodes, but the plot seems to do nothing but slow the already slow series down further. I was hoping it would build on the moment it had at the end of Season 1, but even though the story pics pretty much on the end of that it slowed down again. In my opinion it is fighting hard again for the the number three slot of slowest anime(DBZ, Naruto, and Bleach).<br /> <br /> Not really though I do think the first arc was the best. I like that it added magic and really there is still tons of swordsmen they are just swordfairies now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I read a bit about the next arc and not sure that it is going to live up to the first arc still. I'm kind of disappointed that they are using speed for their version of ever increasing power level. It seems like every challenge is going to be invariably faster than Kirito rather than be an obstacle for a different reason. It is as disappointing as is his ever growing harem that isn't(sort of like Ai Yori Aoshi).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=309865#post309865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know where you are in the series. Personally I'm digging on Log Horizon, though I understand if it's not everyone's cup of tea. Kind of slow paced with lots of world building, politics, economics and round table-type discussions. Also some people really didn't likethe &quot;introduction to MMOs episode&quot; where the new players learn how to party, but I think it should be mandatory watching before anyone plays an MMO (&quot;wait for the tank to get aggro and get out of the fire guy's!&quot;)<br /> <br /> I wasn't as big of a fan of SOA - it just didn't feel as MMO's, probably because it didn't really use any mechanics and Kirito was able to basically solo his way through everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, at some point in typing I hacked off the Season 2 part. I liked Season 1(though I found it a bit too slow at first), but it had a really good momentum going at the end. Then it kind of stumbled, tumbled, and fell into Season two.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T16:00:57-08:00","id":310631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Nasu writing it? He said Fate/Extra CCC was his &quot;magnum opus&quot; for the Fate series and he probably wasn't going to write any other major stories for Fate. But you know how writers often change their minds... </div> </div> </div>It was a false alarm, but Nasu indeed stated he wants to write more Extra, without telling in what form.<br /> <br /> It's Fate milking season anyway. Apocrypha will finish on December and right away Strange/Fake will be released. Apocrypha great though, so I don't mind if they will milk it further and release anime version one day.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T21:57:27-08:00","id":310922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=310577#post310577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, at some point in typing I hacked off the Season 2 part. I liked Season 1(though I found it a bit too slow at first), but it had a really good momentum going at the end. Then it kind of stumbled, tumbled, and fell into Season two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. Yeah, I agree then. Season 2 is by a different company (DEEN) and has a different director, and I think they're still trying to find their pace a bit. Plus, from what I hear this volume is the slowest. It should pick up once they focus on Shirou's raid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:20:39-08:00","id":310982,"title":"","content":"I'm getting a serious itch to reread Angelic Layer. Think I'll do this on Saturday.<br /> <br /> #icchanismyspiritanimal<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(oh god I'm hastagging.)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:10:12-08:00","id":311100,"title":"","content":"DEEN evokes... strong feelings in Type-Moon fandom.<br /> <br /> Just bring it up in Saber FC and see people being &quot;bitter&quot; and complaining Type-Moon neglects them because UBW got ufotable adaptation and HF is scheduled for a one.<br /> <br /> Then rub salt into wounds and bring up possibility of Fate/Apocrypha being animated (which features literal Saber clone, so that only adds spice to the argument) because it sells well as a light novel.<br /> <br /> Or mention Fate/Hollow Ataraxia's hypothetical adaptation, but without SoL, only main plot scenes. Avenger is love, Avenger is life.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't have anything against Saber, but at the largest Western TM forum few waifuists that post in Saber FC drived away genuine Saber fans from posting there and now publically declaring outside Saber FC that you like Saber is as hard decision for some as coming out of closet because Jackinfinite101's and his cult's behavior. Shine on, you crazy diamond, my Skype TM chat got little boring for a while once Mad Jack quitted because we don't &quot;love Saber enough&quot; ;_;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-13-2014, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:41:36-08:00","id":311111,"title":"","content":"I supose I should be reading &quot;Arturia&quot; where you wrote &quot;Saber&quot;. I mean, Saber is a <i>type</i> of Servant. Or is it that fandom is bonkers about Servants with swords in general? I always thought I would like to have a CuChulain heroic spirit as a Berserkr type Servant. His Noble Phantasm would be the reason he was classed as Berserkr (otherwise looking like a Saber or Lancer) his famous war-spasm the Riastrad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:51:40-08:00","id":311121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I supose I should be reading &quot;Arturia&quot; where you wrote &quot;Saber&quot;. I mean, Saber is a type of Servant. Or is it that fandom is bonkers about Servants with swords in general? I always thought I would like to have a CuChulain heroic spirit as a Berserkr type Servant. His Noble Phantasm would be the reason he was classed as Berserkr (otherwise looking like a Saber or Lancer) his famous war-spasm the Riastrad. </div> </div> </div>Ok, I tried to not spoil people, but I guess it's common knowledge already. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes, I mean Arturia. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T08:16:46-08:00","id":311287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=310922#post310922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotcha. Yeah, I agree then. Season 2 is by a different company (DEEN) and has a different director, and I think they're still trying to find their pace a bit. Plus, from what I hear this volume is the slowest. It should pick up once they focus on Shirou's raid.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I'm waiting to see. I wouldn't mind the aside as much if it wasn't trying to be deeper than it seems and actually did something. To me it is like someone was trying to have a deep philosophical discussion about a lollipop. No, really it only takes 3 licks to get to the center of a tootsie pop and then we can move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T10:19:40-08:00","id":311417,"title":"","content":"Sweet Mother of Jesus, Beast Lair's most active poster got permabanned over technicality, 4 active posters, including one who provides all RAWs, made sockpuppets and may get banned, two moonrune readers threathen to leave if those 4 get banned. Indeed, new dawn for BL.<br /> <br /> Now fifth popular poster made a sock. Welp. Gotta see if BL crumbles down over this and people make new forum or migrate to Mobius.<br /> <br /> And my Skype friend, don't get banned, Gio.<br /> <br /> Though one of more level headed and cooler mods said no one will get perma'd over this or at least he will try to make it so with other mod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of dist