iv style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i1153.photobucket.com/albums/p503/thekingofknights/Fanarts/Mordred02_zps0723e670.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Paid 40 dollars for the art, and I don't regret that at all. I do wonder what I will commission next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:07:17-08:00","id":418198,"title":"","content":"This might be the wrong thread, buuuuuut....I wonder if y'all know of a commission-based artist who does anime-style work that wouldn't be out of place in a WoD book, if you can imagine such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:40:48-08:00","id":418251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=418198#post418198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be the wrong thread, buuuuuut....I wonder if y'all know of a commission-based artist who does anime-style work that wouldn't be out of place in a WoD book, if you can imagine such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>there are but most are on pixiv.net and only know Japanese. The problem being that even if they can decipher your bizarre alien language they probably wont do the art for you. There are some though, start looking on pixiv, find an artist you like and send him a message in very plain English or get a buddy who knows basic kana to write your message out for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:00:55-08:00","id":418268,"title":"","content":"I know enough Japanese to probably <i>painfully</i> write a request.<br /> <br /> If you got some people you like in particular, let me know. otherwise, yeah, I'll flip through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T23:21:56-07:00","id":438089,"title":"","content":"I finished Skip Beat!(the anime) a few days ago. For something I avoided for the longest time I loved it. I wasn't really sold on the premise of a girl supporting someone just to find out she had been used the whole time. That and I didn't want to wait for what I assumed was going to be the whole build up and the other half the fall out. I was happily surprised it didn't waste any time with that, but pretty much set it up all quickly to get to the real story. Great story and a ton of laughs. Hate there was only one season. I think I'm going to pick up the manga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T20:11:11-07:00","id":583097,"title":"","content":"So, revival time, with an odd question.<br /> <br /> Can you guys think of an anime movie that was made <i>after </i>its' respective series was produced that is <i>better</i> than it's own series?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T06:10:14-07:00","id":583419,"title":"","content":"Well, let's see. The only thing I can think of off hand is Time of Eve, which was originally a short, 4 episode show. Later they combined the episodes together and added some new material and turned into it a movie. So it was &quot;better&quot; in the sense that it was the original series + extended material. <br /> <br /> Other than that, I would say the two Nanoha movies and the first two Madoka Magica movies might apply. With Madoka they turned the first season into two different movies, and if not better, I feel they're every bit as good as the original series was. <br /> <br /> With the Nanoha movies, they took the each of the two seasons, but them down and turned them into movies. While there was quite a bit lost (due to taking thirteen episode series and crunching them down into 2 hour movies), and while I think ultimately the series were better, the movies are perfectly fine and have some pretty great moments. Ultimately they're fairly comparable to the original series, even if not necessarily &quot;better.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:09:58-07:00","id":585751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=418198#post418198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be the wrong thread, buuuuuut....I wonder if y'all know of a commission-based artist who does anime-style work that wouldn't be out of place in a WoD book, if you can imagine such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I found 'Kemono Inukai' 10-15 years ago, but his personal sites are all in Japaneese, and the one English site shows his last update 2 years ago.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://legacy.shadowlordinc.com/artists/ki_06.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:39:15-07:00","id":668962,"title":"","content":"Has anyone been watching School Live? It has not been what I was expecting, and I mean that in a good way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T17:25:54-07:00","id":669028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=668962#post668962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone been watching School Live? It has not been what I was expecting, and I mean that in a good way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it's pretty fun. <br /> <br /> Spoilered for people who haven't seen the first episode.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">When I watched the first episode, I had no idea what I was getting into and was quite surprised with the twist at the end. I got my friend to watch it. He was like, &quot;Some SoL show?&quot; Though by the end of it he was smiling quite a bit. It was definitely one of the better &quot;surprises&quot; that I've seen in awhile. It's also quite a bit more brutal than I was expecting it to be.<br /> <br /> I had from people that there are some pretty big differences between the anime and the manga, so I started reading the manga and it's true. They changed up the order of events quite a bit in the anime, and some extremely important scenes for character building were skipped over entirely. If you're enjoying the anime, I'd recommend reading the manga for sure as it explores some of the characters and situations a lot better than the anime does.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T04:41:18-07:00","id":669508,"title":"","content":"If anybody hasn't watched Rokka no Yuusha, I would recommend it; it has a distinct visual style, interesting, well-composed action scenes, some pretty good characters, and plays about with its initial apparent generic fantasy story to create a rather compelling mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:28:28-07:00","id":670988,"title":"","content":"Agreed. <br /> <br /> GATE has its moments where a surprising dose of realism creeps in. On the downside, it's doing a bit of the harem thing, of which I'm tired. But on balance, I'd recommend it. (Premise: a dimensional gate opens up between Japan and a fantasy world. An invading army marches through from the fantasy world and promptly gets its butt kicked by the JSDF, which then returns the favor by driving through the gate and seizing the territory surrounding it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T17:12:20-07:00","id":675830,"title":"","content":"Man I have so much catching up to do on the anime front. Good thing I have Netflix and Crunchyroll. Just finished Madoka Magica, now I just have to figure out what to watch next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T11:08:21-07:00","id":676566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=675830#post675830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man I have so much catching up to do on the anime front. Good thing I have Netflix and Crunchyroll. Just finished Madoka Magica, now I just have to figure out what to watch next.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should watch the movie, Madoka Magica Rebellion. Then you can weigh in if you thought it was the perfect way to end the series or of it completely shat all over the entire franchise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T18:35:52-07:00","id":677117,"title":"","content":"Thing of the matter is that it is not the end of the franchise. The movie was made explicitly to open a way to continue the franchise onward along it's central track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T18:50:22-07:00","id":677122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=676566#post676566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should watch the movie, Madoka Magica Rebellion. Then you can weigh in if you thought it was the perfect way to end the series or of it completely shat all over the entire franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, just got done watching it. Honestly I don't see it as an end to the franchise (really either the end of the series or the movie work and I would love to see more material from both worlds). All in all I'm pretty sure we'll probably see some kind of sequel at some point. Heck if Lyrical Nanoha can get as many seasons as it has Madoka can easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:53:02-07:00","id":683619,"title":"","content":"I need a new anime, something awesome, something I can buy on DVD, something that will stroke my hipster boner for how little people have heard of it these days. That last one may or may not actually apply.<br /> <br /> I know, that's incredibly vague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T03:15:23-07:00","id":684181,"title":"","content":"Does it specifically have to be on DVD?<br /> <br /> I don't really involve myself in much online discussion, so I've got a fairly poor barometer for what &quot;people have heard of these days&quot;...<br /> <br /> Maybe Baccano? Or Xam'D? I know those are <i>on</i> DVD...<br /> <br /> Did you ever see Gargantia on the Verdurous Planet? That's a pretty good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:21:51-07:00","id":684471,"title":"","content":"I've got Baccano.<br /> <br /> And I have not seen that on, I'll look into it.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it should be playable on DVD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T15:55:04-07:00","id":687601,"title":"","content":"Wow I'm really late on this one. It totally flew past me without even noticing.<br /> <br /> I admit I've been really bad the last couple years in not buying many of the manga I like. I've been more into gaming or getting my anime fix through Chruncyroll, One that has been really special for me has been Oh My Goddess. When I rediscovered(since at the time I didn't know that G-Force and Robotech were anime) anime the first two I picked up BGC and Oh My Goddess OVAs. I was sold that moment on.<br /> <br /> What brought that about was I just saw that the OMG manga had ended(bet some knew, but as I said I totally missed it). I wasn't reading them as they released in Japan so for me I guess you could say it just ended in September. It wasn't till well after the OVA that I found out that OMG had a manga. That moment I bought all the past ones I could and kept up with it and comping at the bit when I had to wait between paychecks or other things. As of late I didn't keep up as I said and I kind of took it for granted it would be there waiting for me to pick it up. It was this warm blanket I could go to whenever I needed some warm fuzzies and I'm more than a little sad to see it go(gone). :'(<br /> <br /> I'm a little verklempt now. Garlic, stinky plant or god's gift to pizza? Discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T22:53:53-08:00","id":824838,"title":"","content":"So, I've been watching, and for the most part, enjoying Mirai Nikki, aka Future Diary. Essentially, it follows Yukiteru, your standard milquetoast, weak-willed anime protagonist. He compulsively keeps notes on everything around him, and occasionally talks to God (he's not insane, he just pretends). Until it turns out that God is real and is running a game where the last survivor takes over His station. Yuki is pretty useless, until he hooks up with Yuno, a classmate with an obsessive psychotic streak a mile wide. She loves him, in the &quot;one day she will kill him and wear his skin as clothes&quot; tradition. It is played every bit as horrific as it should be, and most of the series is <i>awesome</i>.<br /> <br /> However, the last couple episodes I've watched (11 and 12) were really weak. Characters were acting really OOC for no readily apparent reason, I'm pretty sure the plot itself didn't hang together, and it really seems the main draw of the show has flipped without any particularly clear reason. I'll keep watching, but I'm kind of disappointed with the turn of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T04:10:07-08:00","id":834938,"title":"","content":"Future Diary was one of those shows with a ton of potential that just horribly fell apart as it went on. Unfortunately it felt like the author didn't really know where to take things. Too bad, the first 1/3rd was pretty amazing.<br /> <br /> So, for this season, I'm finding it pretty slow. The only show I'm watching is Pandora in the Crimson Shell: Ghost Urn. It's by the author of Excel Saga, who teamed up with Shiro Masamune of Ghost in the Shell.<br /> <br /> Kokaku no Pandora (as it's normally abbreviated to) is basically a girl meets girl story, though one of the girls us a full body cyborg while the other is a robot. The show is chock full of references to Ghost in the Shell, so many you can think of it as a semi-lighthearted prequel. It's also got a few references to Excel Saga hidden here and there.<br /> <br /> The show obviously has a low budget, but the animation team does a great job animating things in ways that are fun and can work within the limited budget they have available. It's pretty clear the animation team enjoys working on the show and they manage to push that energy through to the viewers.<br /> <br /> The show is rather lewd (one of the characters, Clarion, has a port in her lower abdomen that pops out and the other girl has to insert her finger to link up) though since the characters have bodies like Barbie dolls (complete with obviously artificial joints) I find it tends to be a bit more humorous than overly sexy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T08:58:57-08:00","id":835807,"title":"","content":"Are there any reasons why there are so many &quot;I'm an average spiky hair otaku who is now trapped in MORPG land&quot; anime in these past few years ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:18:09-08:00","id":835825,"title":"","content":"Pretty easy to write escapist fiction that resonates with the target audience. &quot;I'm not good at real life stuff, but I play video games so I'd be awesome in a video game based world.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's been a few in that genre I thought were good like Log Horizon, but they actually focus heavily on the video game mechanics, rather than just including them as an afterthought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-23-2016, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T20:02:16-08:00","id":839641,"title":"","content":"I've watched the two seasons of Magi that exist and they were pretty good, wish there was a third season. Little Witch Academia and its sequel were great too. Fate Zero and Fate Unlimited Blade Works from ufotable were amazing as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T20:44:56-08:00","id":839654,"title":"","content":"I've been watching \u201cERASED\u201d on Crunchyroll. Wow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T13:42:51-08:00","id":844127,"title":"","content":"Hai To Gensou No Grimgar (Grimgar Of Ashes And Fantasy) is a comparatively somber fantasy experience in this anime season that does a lot of good things. The devil is in the details - how logical consequences follow, how the characters are akward and fallible and lost, how they're a bunch of scrubs trying to get by, how the monsters have as much personhood as them, and how they deal with loss and pain from the harshness of the world. It's got some lovely waterfaded backgrounds and climactic music too. Of note is its slow and thorough pacing that works really well with the atmosphere. I could go into detail, but describing it in many words may be more difficult than in few. So instead I just recommend giving a few episodes a watch to understand the experience.<br /> <br /> On the flip side of fantasy anime, Kono Subarashi Sekai Ni Shukufuku Wo, or KonoSuba, is hilarious. Not only because every character has a broken personality of the ridiculous sort that all interact in an explosive fashion, but because the comedy seems intent on ridiculing cocky premises quite handily and nothing ever seems to go well for anyone. Of course, humor is subjective, but when KonoSuba comes to life I know I'm going to enjoy a shameless comedy of errors.<br /> <br /> More standard fare but enjoyable in the ways they're not:<br /> <br /> Ao No Kanata No Four Rhythm pleasantly surprised me because I wasn't expecting the main female character's lovable spunk (in addition to her airheadedness), and despite looking kinda typical (it IS a visual novel adaptation), all the developments and important characterization in the cast have been really well spread out among their various relationships. This is not a &quot;only the male MC engages with the issues of the other characters&quot; situation. Much to the contrary, he has a strong supportive role but the limelight has consistently been on the female members of the Flying Circus club, the people they meet, and the issues they have and how they help each other (and are helped by the supporting cast).<br /> <br /> Shoujo-Tachi Wa Kouya Wo Mesazu (Girls Beyond The Wasteland) is an interesting and kind of self-parodying sort of story, given it's about a group of friends working to make a visual novel, and is itself going to be released as a visual novel soon. It seems pretty typical and I've heard people say they weren't interested because it seemed like a show with harem tones. Much like similar comments about 4Rhythm, I don't know how they got that idea. There has been an episode focused on a character's hesitant romantic interest in her friend, but there's a lot more to the relations of the cast - and indeed to how they work together and manage to organize themselves - than romance. The difficulties they face in a project like this, both internal and external, are given a fair bit of importance, both on their own and in how they affect the small cast of slightly quirky characters. And although that quality isn't always there, the show has shown to be extremely good at &quot;show, don't tell&quot; as early as the very first episode, when we got to know our main character and his defining traits by following his day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:39:52-07:00","id":915248,"title":"","content":"I am quite enjoying this show Twin-Star Exorcists. It's visually dynamic, I find most of the characters reasonably compelling, and there's enough novelty in the premise to have caught my attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T04:26:31-07:00","id":915509,"title":"","content":"One thing I'll say as a small note of something I like in the show, simply because I've seen a couple of things reminding me of it:<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the protagonists tends to fight in her school uniform, and yet this isn't used as an excuse to titillate the audience on several counts. Not only is it a fairly long skirt, and not only does she wear shorts under it, but none of the shots are ever framed in a manner that gives the audience an angle on anything.<br /> <br /> This extends to the point where one scene including an instance of the male protagonist briefly catching a glance up her skirt (which is not particularly contrived, as these things go), it is not a glance that is extended in the least to the viewer.<br /> <br /> It's a detail that I appreciate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T11:24:21-07:00","id":994125,"title":"","content":"This season blows. The only show worth watching has been Getsuyoubi no Tawawa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T14:30:21-07:00","id":994225,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this season is pretty disappointing. <br /> <br /> I'm only watching two shows. Brave Witches, a spin-off of Strike Witches, though so far it feels pretty unremarkable and the cast isn't anywhere near as interesting as Strike Witches was.<br /> <br /> The other show I'm watching is Vivid Strike, a spinoff of Nanoha Vivid. It's actually pretty good and feels like a nice spiritual successor to the older Nanoha franchise, though this one focuses more on the characters being magical MMA fighters with lots of weightlifting and training montages rather than on being purely magical girls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T15:17:04-07:00","id":994237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=994225#post994225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this season is pretty disappointing.<br /> <br /> I'm only watching two shows. Brave Witches, a spin-off of Strike Witches, though so far it feels pretty unremarkable and the cast isn't anywhere near as interesting as Strike Witches was.<br /> <br /> The other show I'm watching is Vivid Strike, a spinoff of Nanoha Vivid. It's actually pretty good and feels like a nice spiritual successor to the older Nanoha franchise, though this one focuses more on the characters being magical MMA fighters with lots of weightlifting and training montages rather than on being purely magical girls.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah I saw the shoe locker scene on /a/. Jesus. I didn't pick up brave witches but Its mostly because its one of the few anime I really like to sit and watch all the episodes at once like some kind of drug addict. <br /> <br /> I just finally caught all the way up with the monogatari series. The nearest showing for Kizumonogatari is about 8 hours away though so I'm not going to get to see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T15:31:11-07:00","id":994242,"title":"","content":"The shoe-locker scene was pretty harsh, but then Nanoha has always been surprisingly dark, with characters getting tortured, seriously injured and killed. The most recent series, Vivid, was much more &quot;cute&quot; and &quot;hugboxy&quot; and I think in the years since StrikerS came out some people forgot how dark the Nanoha franchise could be at times. <br /> <br /> As for Monogatari what did you think of it? Personally I probably rate it as one of my three favorite anime series. I think it has really great characters, each one with memorable scenes, quirks and personality. Plus the series has some of the best dialogue I've heard in an anime series, and I'm a sucker for good dialogue and witty banter. Further, SHAFT's visuals manage to make even the random conversations visually engaging, and I think the music score is darn near perfect for setting or enhancing the mood. <br /> <br /> The story is typically a bit weak, but then I feel that the story is more just an excuse for Nisoisin to write dialogue and interactions for the characters. That's the core of the show, and the &quot;why&quot; is largely just a vehicle to set up the chance for those characters to interact with one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:12:21-07:00","id":994261,"title":"","content":"For monogatari I became attached to the characters back with Bakemonogatari and honestly my opinion hasn't changed much involving them. The main reason I watched it all the way through was to see what would happen to my favorite characters. I honestly couldn't care about Nadeko. She didn't become likable to me until she became a homicidal snake goddess. Kanbaru and Hachikuji always had my favorite stories. Senjougahara kind of seemed to fall to the wayside as the stories progressed. I also liked how things in Owarimonogatari and Koyomimonogatari actually occurred in previous installments as well. I didn't care much for Ougi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:39:15-07:00","id":997864,"title":"","content":"Hachikuji was my favorite character in the Monogotarari series. I thought she had the best interactions with Arararagi and their back and forth banter was great. I especially loved her, &quot;The courage to...&quot; conversation that they had. <br /> <br /> So, I just got finished reading the first two stories in the visual novel series World End Economica. <br /> <br /> The setting is fairly interesting - it takes place several centuries from now on the moon. The main character is essentially a run-away hobo who makes money by playing the stock market, making sure to have just enough to survive while investing everything else. There's lot of interesting stock market analysis and problems, and the story revolves around the character trying to make a fortune. Even as someone who was never terribly interested in the stock market, the writing managed to make everything look neat and exciting.<br /> <br /> The story played up the science fiction elements fairly well, and one of the bigger themes in the story were that of the moneyed elite and the poor who have to bow to their whims. Money makes the world go around, as they say. There was also an interesting tangent on religious faith. One of the major characters in the story is a Christian who helps the main character out quite a bit and it was nice to see the Christian religion to have such a positive portrayal. It also helped to shine a different aspect on the otherwise &quot;pro-money&quot; segments of the rest of the story and on several occasions pushed the idea that money was both good and bad - that it can solve problems but also creates problems.<br /> <br /> The second story takes place several years after the first - the story is quite a bit darker and the themes are far less optimistic and adult than they originally were. The main character has undergone major changes due to events that happened at the end of the first game, and a lot of the story on this one is him trying to come to terms with what happened and his decision on whether to move on or try to go back. The second game had more of a &quot;detective&quot; or &quot;investigative&quot; mood to it than the earlier game, and the focus on the stock market was less important.<br /> <br /> Still, it did a nice job of continuing the story in a direction I was not expecting and has me eagerly looking forward to the third (and I believe final) installment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:52:33-07:00","id":997871,"title":"","content":"yeah I've got World End Economica on steam from like 3 years ago but I've yet to read it. I'm currently reading Dracu-Riot! and when I finish it I'll probably try Rewrite again. I just finished KonoSuba and I'm going to watch Outbreak Company next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:54:48-07:00","id":997932,"title":"","content":"Konosuba was pretty 10/10. I haven't watched a series that funny in a long time. Of course, right after watching it most of people in my group decided that their next character is going to be Megumin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T16:30:07-07:00","id":997950,"title":"","content":"I liked it. I've got the first few LNs downloaded now so I'll probably check them out. We're also going to get another Highschool DxD anime soonish (which will be faithful to source material unlike S3) so I'm looking forward to that. New season of precure looks like its gonna be super qt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:18:01-07:00","id":999029,"title":"","content":"Drifters and Hibike Euphonium 2 are the shows I've been following most attentively this season. Hibike is consistently incredibly high in production values and enriched by characters easy to relate to, so I wholeheartedly recommend it in the same breath as I do the first season. Drifters is a party of Kohta Hirano's detailed gore-heavy action and atmospheric characters, but it also engages with surprisingly realistic and brutal tactics as well as philosophy on war and death. Our main group of protagonists brings together a set of very different skills and values, and their effect on the environment that surrounds them is proving quite interesting to watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:50:52-08:00","id":1002435,"title":"","content":"This season, only Bungou Stray Dogs 2 and Fune bo Amu managed to grab our attention. Thankfully, these two are still here to keep us in good anime drive, started by Assasination Classroom, followed by Erased, sustained by Bungou and peaking at ReZero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:00:34-08:00","id":1002439,"title":"","content":"I was genuinely surprised with Re:Zero. I started off being fairly ho-hum. By the end of the first arc I was enjoying it. By the end of the second arc I was liking the main character quite a bit. Then with the third arc and the second season I started really hating the main character, almost to the point that I wanted to drop the series. But then the MC had a good arc and ended up redeeming himself (except for his choice of romantic interests, BOO) and by the end of it I think Subaru was my favorite main character that I have seen in a show in many years. <br /> <br /> We actually got some real character growth and development slowly over the course of a season, which is all-too rare in Japanese media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T19:40:28-08:00","id":1003208,"title":"","content":"Mahou Shoujo Ikusai Keikaku (or, in English, Magical Girl Raising Project) is a magical girl show in the spirit of Puella Magi Madoka Magica. The premise is that sixteen players of a social game about Magical Girls are given the opportunity to become magical girls for real. Then they're told that the number has to be reduced to eight, turning it into a sort of Reality TV Show where each week the lowest-scoring magical girl gets kicked out of the project. <br /> <br /> So far, I've been liking it. My main quarrel with it thus far has been that some of the characters have departed sooner than I would have liked \u2014 but then, most of the characters are written well enough that I'd be sad to see them go no matter how long it took. Whereas others have no business sticking around as long as they have\u2026<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T21:13:10-08:00","id":1003232,"title":"","content":"It looked like one of those shows where all the characters I enjoyed would be dead or gone by episode 6, so I was going to wait until it was finished, see what happens and then decide whether I wanted to watch it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:19:41-08:00","id":1003602,"title":"","content":"Well, it <i>is</i> essentially a cross between Madoka and Bokurano. That said, the death toll is remarkably light so far, well under the number of episodes released. And in keeping with its Bokurano-like elements, what deaths have happened have been driven by character and plot rather than spectacle. If they're going to wrap this up in a dozen episodes or so, they're going to have to pick up the pace; or else there will be a lot more survivors than I anticipate. But if you're avoiding it because you don't want to watch something where half the cast disappears by the mid-point, don't worry about it; that's not happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:03:07-07:00","id":1069683,"title":"","content":"So, this anime season is winding down. I watched several shows and there were 3 that I ended up enjoying quite a bit. <br /> <br /> The first was the second season of Konosuba. Unfortunately it was made by a different studio than season one and had a new director. The source material was good enough that it managed to hold the show together, but the 2nd season was strictly worse than the 1st in pretty much every way. Still entertaining, but nowhere near as good. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second show I enjoyed a lot was Kobayashi's Dragon Maid. One day the main character, Kobyashi wakes up, and finds out that the night before while out drinking, she had encountered a dragon and invited it to come live with her. The dragon, Tohru, had been near death and Kobayashi saved her, and so the dragon fell in love with her. The show is a mix of romance, comfyness and comedy. <br /> <br /> The big three plot threads through the show are that Kobayashi has spent most of her life focused on her job. She only has one friend, doesn't have any real hobbies and doesn't really do awhole lot besides work. So Tohru is often getting her to come out of her comfort zones and do things she's not used to. Meanwhile Tohru has spent most of her life (on another world) being hunted by (and hunting) humans. While she idolizes Kobayashi, she still generally dislikes other humans, so a fair amount of the show is her dealing with that issue. The last big plot revolves around another dragon who moves in with them named Kanna. Kanna is is a young dragon (only a few centuries old) and she's more interested in getting along with humans. She eventually ends up attending school and she and the friends she makes there form the last big pillar the show is based around. <br /> <br /> Overall I ended up enjoying it quite a bit. It had very nice animation, it never got overly series, and it was rather refreshing to have a show that follows an adult, female character (that's pretty uncommon in anime).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The last show (and the one I ended up enjoying the most) came out of nowhere. I only started watching it three weeks ago because I heard people saying good things about. It's called Kemono Friends. I was avoiding it because the show is CG and honestly it's <i>bad</i> CG. Really bad. And it's based on one of those phone games. Only the phone game was shut down several months before the show came out. I guess they decided to finish the show and release it because they had already put so much work into it. <br /> <br /> So when I saw people talking about how good it was, and people saying that the show was insanely popular in Japan and had led to a huge burst in people going to zoos I figured I'd go ahead and watch it just to see why it was so popular. <br /> <br /> The show takes place in Japari Park, an abandoned animal theme park. At some point monsters appeared and began attacking people. Humans abandoned the park, but at the same time some of the animals will occasionally turn into animal-people who call themselves Friends. <br /> <br /> The story follows a girl who suddenly wakes up in the park. She has no memories and no idea who or what she is. She meets an animal-girl named Serval who helps her try to figure out what kind of an animal she is. The girl, Kaban, can't run fast or climb trees or do anything else, so the two of them set off to find the library. Of course, the main character is a human, and in Japari Park humans are considered almost mythic beings who haven't been seen before.<br /> <br /> The show is generally episodic and follows the same basic premise. Kaban and Serval travel to a new part of the park, meet new Friends and help them solve their problems. Meanwhile the episode is punctuated by short clips from animal experts talking about the animals who show up in that episode. Each of the individual Friend's problems however are so different, and the areas are so different, that even though they share the same premise each episode feels very different from one another.<br /> <br /> The surprising thing about the show was how subtly dark everything was. They're in an abandoned amusement park filled with monsters that are trying to eat them, and everything is slowly collapsing and falling apart. As Kaban and Serval travel through the part, they slowly begin to figure out what happened to other people, and sometimes receive old video or audio files from one of the park workers. So while the show is primarily about Kaban's journey of self-discovery to find out who and what she is, it's also about what Japari Park is and what happened to it, plus of course they meet other Friends and help them, created a nice layered narrative framework for the show. <br /> <br /> Really, once I ended up getting past the bad CG, I ended up enjoying this series a heck of a lot more than I ever imagined I would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T18:20:32-07:00","id":1069760,"title":"","content":"acca 13-ku kansatsu-ka ended. I don't know how much sandwich bread is going to fill that void but I'll be damned if I don't try and find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T10:47:26-07:00","id":1072090,"title":"","content":"So, as I'm sure people know, the first new episode of Attack on Titan in four years came out yesterday.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo commemorate the occasion, I finally put together a comedic little video that I've had in mind for several years, and intermittently working on for a few months.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhy not give it a look, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (minor spoiler warning for the end of the first season; it's about four seconds)<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio vide