],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T17:47:30-07:00","id":1212855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1072090#post1072090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(minor spoiler warning for the end of the first season; it's about four seconds)<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HmT7BztvcCY\" data-code=\"HmT7BztvcCY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HmT7BztvcCY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;It'll be okay&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> No, no it won't! Shit is getting wrecked in the manga, right now!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T19:57:41-07:00","id":1212899,"title":"","content":"Taking this conversation here so as not to continue derailing the You Know What I Hate thread...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3132-you-know-what-i-hate-mk-i?p=1212850#post1212850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, I used to like Naruto and thought it had decent potential. But then came Filler Hell, and after that, the endless barrage of plot holes and inconsistencies that made up Shippuden. Seriously, the later half of the series played out like the creator developed ADHD and had no idea what direction he wanted to take the story in.<br /> <br /> I've taken to calling the Sharingan the 'Batman Eyes' because they have a power uniquely tailored to virtually any threat or situation that they find themselves in. And yet, somehow, the first half of the series claims the Byakugan's oracular abilities surpass those of the Sharingan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was a promising series that suffered from the same issue that plagues pretty much every decent shonen. Hell, shojo too. Pressure on the author to crank out an incredible amount of content on a ridiculous schedule. Inevitably, the author extends well beyond their initial concept and has to fly by the seat of their pants, leading to losing the theme, introducing major inconsistencies and loose plot threads, and of course the power escalation problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/3132-you-know-what-i-hate-mk-i?p=1212850#post1212850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stopped reading after Tobi was unmasked. That reveal took the last centimeters worth of rope I was willing to give the series and went off to find the tallest tree in the forest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I thought that was painfully predictable. His mask has one eye hole and his alias is an angram for his real name with an extra o (or a missing o, depending on how you look at it.) That one was right up there with the 4th hokage being Natuto\u2019s dad in terms of \u201creveals\u201d everyone saw coming years in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-28-2018, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:25:36-07:00","id":1212905,"title":"","content":"The thing that gets me when I go back and watch Naruto is the sexism. I just can't unsee it and while I can overlook a lot in the name of mindless entertainment, I can't get past that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:52:28-07:00","id":1212918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212899#post1212899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking this conversation here so as not to continue derailing the You Know What I Hate thread...<br /> <br /> <br /> Really? I thought that was painfully predictable. His mask has one eye hole and his alias is an angram for his real name with an extra o (or a missing o, depending on how you look at it.) That one was right up there with the 4th hokage being Natuto\u2019s dad in terms of \u201creveals\u201d everyone saw coming years in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *Inhales deeply*<br /> <br /> Ooookay, I guess I have to break out this tangent a second time (posted it originally on a SoFurry journal).<br /> <br /> Let's start with the fact Obito had 50% of his body <i><b>vertically</b></i> crushed under a boulder roughly 5 times his size. The fact he was even conscious enough to speak was nothing short of a miracle, not to mention forming complete sentences with only half a brain. And he was alive long enough for Rin to perform amateur eye surgery without succumbing to further blood loss. And after all of that, he somehow manages to survive long enough for Zetsu to exfiltrate him to the mountains (again, with 50% of his body crushed) and undergo an experimental procedure to splice his DNA with Hashirama's cells.<br /> <br /> This is a CHILD, a 10 year old boy and one who is confirmed to be a pretty crappy ninja at that. Naruto and Gaara at the very least had demonic spirits to explain their unnatural endurance. What the hell was going on with Obito!?<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212905#post1212905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that gets me when I go back and watch Naruto is the sexism. I just can't unsee it and while I can overlook a lot in the name of mindless entertainment, I can't get past that</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No, you're not just seeing things. It's pretty obvious the females were almost exclusively throw away characters. The only noticeable exception being the Sasori fight, and I think that's only because there were no men around to bail them out. Oh, that's right, Sasori just spontaneously decided he wanted to die out of friggin nowhere. Thus contradicting his entire philosophy on what constitutes as 'artistic'</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:11:13-07:00","id":1212923,"title":"","content":"Oh, I know. I just find it extremely jarring because I don't remember it being that bad when I first watched Naruto in about 2009 as a university student. Yeah, it seemed like the female characters got a raw deal, but they were interesting characters and honestly I still love a lot of them. At the time my thoughts were basically &quot;this is a show aimed at boys, so that's a shitty, but I've been seen worse.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I can't watch the match between Sakura and Ino at all. The entire thing is so dumb and Sakura has legit Stockholm Syndrome and that was before the writer said something along the lines of &quot;it would be a betrayal of her character for her to give up on her childhood crush.&quot; Sooooooo stupid and patriarchal, plus a waste of characters who could have been strong female leads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:43:34-07:00","id":1212931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212923#post1212923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know. I just find it extremely jarring because I don't remember it being that bad when I first watched Naruto in about 2009 as a university student. Yeah, it seemed like the female characters got a raw deal, but they were interesting characters and honestly I still love a lot of them. At the time my thoughts were basically &quot;this is a show aimed at boys, so that's a shitty, but I've been seen worse.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I can't watch the match between Sakura and Ino at all. The entire thing is so dumb and Sakura has legit Stockholm Syndrome and that was before the writer said something along the lines of &quot;it would be a betrayal of her character for her to give up on her childhood crush.&quot; Sooooooo stupid and patriarchal, plus a waste of characters who could have been strong female leads.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The moment when Sakura absolutely infuriated me was when she tries to launch her own mission to stop Sasuke's attack on the village. Why don't we go down the list of fuck ups she made during that moment?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>1st of all:</b> The village is under threat of an impending attack and is therefor placed on high alert.<br /> <br /> Being fully aware of this, Sakura personally decides to assemble a team of Chunin and Jonin rank ninjas to go intercept and eliminate Sasuke.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2nd:</b> Half way to the intercept point, Sakura incapacitates the team that SHE PUT TOGETHER because in her own words <i>&quot;she had to take care of this herself.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So now, there's about 5 or 6 experienced ninjas just passed out in the middle of the forest where enemies could attack at any moment!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>3rd:</b> When she finally does reach Sasuke, who at this point in the series has tried to kill her and Naruto multiple times, she loses her nerve and says she can't do it. Even when she has a golden opportunity to do so!<br /> <br /> So thanks, Sakura. Thank you for wasting our time and endangering the lives of your own villagers. I'm glad you became a medical ninja, because it is the only thing keeping you from being completely fucking useless!<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, what's that? Naruto and Sasuke both obtained god powers and can resurrect people with no negative consequences?<br /> <br /> *Sakura retires as a ninja to become a single mother*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-21-2018, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:18:50-07:00","id":1212956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212918#post1212918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Inhales deeply*<br /> <br /> Ooookay, I guess I have to break out this tangent a second time (posted it originally on a SoFurry journal).<br /> <br /> Let's start with the fact Obito had 50% of his body <i><b>vertically</b></i> crushed under a boulder roughly 5 times his size. The fact he was even conscious enough to speak was nothing short of a miracle, not to mention forming complete sentences with only half a brain. And he was alive long enough for Rin to perform amateur eye surgery without succumbing to further blood loss. And after all of that, he somehow manages to survive long enough for Zetsu to exfiltrate him to the mountains (again, with 50% of his body crushed) and undergo an experimental procedure to splice his DNA with Hashirama's cells.<br /> <br /> This is a CHILD, a 10 year old boy and one who is confirmed to be a pretty crappy ninja at that. Naruto and Gaara at the very least had demonic spirits to explain their unnatural endurance. What the hell was going on with Obito!?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... It\u2019s a shonen. People surviving absurd bodily trauma with nothing to show for it but a few superficial scars that really just make them look cooler isn\u2019t just normal, it\u2019s expected. It\u2019s like with super hero comics, the only people for whom death is permanent are the protagonist\u2019s loved ones, and injuries only have long-term consequences when it\u2019s narratively convenient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-29-2018, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:24:19-07:00","id":1212957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212923#post1212923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know. I just find it extremely jarring because I don't remember it being that bad when I first watched Naruto in about 2009 as a university student. Yeah, it seemed like the female characters got a raw deal, but they were interesting characters and honestly I still love a lot of them. At the time my thoughts were basically &amp;quot;this is a show aimed at boys, so that's a shitty, but I've been seen worse.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Now I can't watch the match between Sakura and Ino at all. The entire thing is so dumb and Sakura has legit Stockholm Syndrome and that was before the writer said something along the lines of &amp;quot;it would be a betrayal of her character for her to give up on her childhood crush.&amp;quot; Sooooooo stupid and patriarchal, plus a waste of characters who could have been strong female leads.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely sexist and dumb, and I think it ultimately stems from the same problem as Obito being Tobi and the 4th hokage being Naruto\u2019s dad. Same with Naruto and Hinata ending up together. These are all things that the author decided on way ahead of time, and he wasn\u2019t going to let any of the other shenanigans he wrote in the mean time to appease his editors wasn\u2019t going to change that.<br /> <br /> People make the same complaint about the epilogue of Harry Potter. Fortunately, in that case JK happened to make the right narrative decision, and only changed her mind under pressure from fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:49:08-07:00","id":1212964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212957#post1212957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is absolutely sexist and dumb, and I think it ultimately stems from the same problem as Obito being Tobi and the 4th hokage being Naruto\u2019s dad. Same with Naruto and Hinata ending up together. These are all things that the author decided on way ahead of time, and he wasn\u2019t going to let any of the other shenanigans he wrote in the mean time to appease his editors wasn\u2019t going to change that.<br /> <br /> People make the same complaint about the epilogue of Harry Potter. Fortunately, in that case JK happened to make the right narrative decision, and only changed her mind under pressure from fans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Speaking of Hinata, did her sister ever receive the traditional curse mark the rest of the branch family did?<br /> <br /> I don't remember it ever being confirmed in the original story. Or if Hinata decided to abolish the practice after becoming the new head of the family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:58:04-07:00","id":1212966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212956#post1212956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s like with super hero comics, the only people for whom death is permanent are the protagonist\u2019s loved ones, and injuries only have long-term consequences when it\u2019s narratively convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was Naruto plotted to be an ongoing story telling tales in the life of Naruto, or with a mostly fleshed out beginning, middle and end?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T05:26:24-07:00","id":1213017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212966#post1212966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was Naruto plotted to be an ongoing story telling tales in the life of Naruto, or with a mostly fleshed out beginning, middle and end?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I heard a rumor years ago that Naruto was originally supposed to be a story about wizards and that Sasuke wasn't even planned to be a character. But the creator later changed it to ninjas and added in a rival character for Naruto because his editors gave him the Toriyama treatment or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:04:42-07:00","id":1213028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213017#post1213017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I heard a rumor years ago that Naruto was originally supposed to be a story about wizards and that Sasuke wasn't even planned to be a character. But the creator later changed it to ninjas and added in a rival character for Naruto because his editors gave him the Toriyama treatment or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Immediately runs off to go watch <i>Fairy Tail</i>*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T07:22:52-07:00","id":1213050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213028#post1213028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Immediately runs off to go watch <i>Fairy Tail</i>*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Don't do it! Don't do it!<br /> <br /> <br /> It's the climax of Bleach, all over again!<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, why dose everybody hate the lizardmen arc from Overlord?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://t00.deviantart.net/XD9q7318Q43vKBWOi4LhCV_9o7g=/fit-in/700x350/filters:fixed_height(100,100):origin()/pre00/b77e/th/pre/f/2018/038/7/1/overlord_ii_crusch_lulu_zaryusu_shasha_2_by_giuseppedirosso-dc2fvqx.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Only a sick, depraved monster wouldn't love best waifu!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-29-2018, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:35:46-07:00","id":1213068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212905#post1212905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that gets me when I go back and watch Naruto is the sexism. I just can't unsee it and while I can overlook a lot in the name of mindless entertainment, I can't get past that</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sadly that's an issue with Shounen series in general. For the most part in Shounen series, female characters are just eye candy, a love interest or only there to assist the male characters. When you look at most Shonen series (Naruto, One Piece, Bleach, Hunter x Hunter, Kenshin, etc) you find this pattern in the treatment of female characters over and over again.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are some exceptions, like in One Piece we had Big Mom who is one of the most powerful people in the world. Or Fairy Tail which at least had Erza as the token badass female and who was probably the strongest and most interesting person in the series.<br /> <br /> But Shounen series like Medaka Box, with a number of very strong, very important female characters who are well fleshed out in their motivations, personalities and receive as much screen time as the male characters are incredibly rare. Honestly I can't think of many others off-hand - Binbougami Ga, maybe Soul Eater, that's honestly about it.<br /> <br /> Sadly if you're looking for well written female characters you're just not really going to find them in most Shounen series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:46:49-07:00","id":1213072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213050#post1213050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, why dose everybody hate the lizardmen arc from Overlord?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't hate it, exactly. But I was watching Overlord to see Ainz steamroll everyone, and instead those episodes spent a lot of time building up these lizard characters and their relationships, even though you knew they were going to get steamrolled. In fact, I assumed all of them were going to die, so I didn't let myself get emotionally invested in any of them to begin with. So basically my whole attitude throughout that arc was, &quot;Can we get this over with already, because all of them are going to die anyway, and instead move on to the more important things?&quot; <br /> <br /> Maybe I just went into it with the wrong attitude. The second Arc with Sebas being a Hero of Justice around town was pretty amusing though and I enjoyed it a lot more.<br /> <br /> I'll admit though, the lizard-girl-plant-monster was pretty cute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:53:34-07:00","id":1213078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213068#post1213068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of course, there are some exceptions, like in One Piece we had Big Mom who is one of the most powerful people in the world. </div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forget Boa Hancock, who can pretty much one shot the majority of the male characters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or Perona, who can strip her opponents of the will to fight back<br /> <br /> <br /> Or Sugar, who's the first person in the series that made me exclaim <i>&quot;PLEASE NERF!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:18:51-07:00","id":1213100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1212966#post1212966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was Naruto plotted to be an ongoing story telling tales in the life of Naruto, or with a mostly fleshed out beginning, middle and end?</div> </div> </div> </div>An ongoing story. Pretty much anything published in Shonen Jump magazine has to be an ongoing story, as they do weekly serials that continue based on popularity. So as long as your series keeps getting votes, you need to keep writing chapters. It\u2019s actually a huge problem in the manga industry that mangaka are pressured to produce content at an absurd schedule with no definite end point. And it\u2019s why all the best manga go on way too long and end up a mess, because the author is pretty much just winging it week to week and getting no downtime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213017#post1213017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard a rumor years ago that Naruto was originally supposed to be a story about wizards and that Sasuke wasn't even planned to be a character. But the creator later changed it to ninjas and added in a rival character for Naruto because his editors gave him the Toriyama treatment or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. You\u2019re actually conflating two different stories. The original concept that eventually became Naruto was a cooking manga about a boy who worked at a ramen shop. Pretty much everything about that concept ended up getting scrapped except the main character\u2019s name and brash personality. But that\u2019s why Naruto is obsessed with ramen.<br /> <br /> He also had a separate concept for a manga about a boy (who also had a similar design and personality to Naruto) who went to a school for wizards. But then Harry Potter came out and he (or maybe his editors) decided not to go forward with that idea because it would likely be viewed as imitating Harry Potter.<br /> <br /> The Toriyama treatment is pretty much industry standard, especially for shonen jump and shojo beat manga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:30:05-07:00","id":1213111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213078#post1213078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget Boa Hancock, who can pretty much one shot the majority of the male characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My issue with Hancock is that at this point in the series, her character and personality is basically just, &quot;I love Luffy a whole lot,&quot; which is unfortunate since she was an interesting character with a pretty dark past. Taking a cool female character and turning her into a one-note comedic love interest irks me. But, to be fair this is One Piece and there are lots of characters (males and females) who are basically one-note, so I'm willing to accept it.<br /> <br /> That said though you're right in that there have been female characters in the series, some of them with pretty powerful abilities (like, all things considered Shirahoshi the mermaid princess probably has the strongest power in the setting - to the point that she's considered one of the three great weapons of destruction).<br /> <br /> What made Big Mom stand out to me though is that this is the first time we've seen a female character as the primary antagonist of an arc. Other female antagonists have always had a secondary role to the primary arc's antagonist (Robin/Crocodile, Perona/Moriah, Monet/Caesar, Sugar/Doflamingo). Big Mom though is the absolutely the main antagonist for the arc. Further she's also one of the first enemies that Luffy has just turned tail and run from, without trying to fight, because he realized how thoroughly outmatched he was.<br /> <br /> And to be fair this isn't something that is uniquely related to One Piece but rather it's something that's true for many Shounen series. Even if there may be female characters, some of whom are fairly powerful, they're rarely major antagonists on their own. I'm guessing this is because then the author has the issue of depicting the hero fighting the female and in the process depicting violence against women. When a Shounen series does do this the author will typically try to find a way to mitigate it (making the female ugly or monstrous, which is itself problematic) or having other side characters (who are often females themselves or anti-heroes who can do things the main character can't, like beat up women) fight her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-29-2018, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T12:23:18-07:00","id":1213146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213100#post1213100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An ongoing story. Pretty much anything published in Shonen Jump magazine has to be an ongoing story, as they do weekly serials that continue based on popularity. So as long as your series keeps getting votes, you need to keep writing chapters. It\u2019s actually a huge problem in the manga industry that mangaka are pressured to produce content at an absurd schedule with no definite end point. And it\u2019s why all the best manga go on way too long and end up a mess, because the author is pretty much just winging it week to week and getting no downtime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the creators own their creations or is it Shonen Jump? I take it the creators don't have much say when it comes to merchandise?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/B7StHGv.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> It's a known problem in the west, too, though many adapt to it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The sexism thing has been one of the hard walls for me when it comes to manga I've attempted to get started. Power levels don't really bother me, though obviously you want some sort of growth in your protagonists. In a curve, not a 'yesterday I was an average high school student, now I'm Unstoppable McKickasson,' or at least with some curveballs thrown at Mr. McKickasson. It's not really something to 'just' point at manga at, though, we have big series of novels that are styled similarly, like Wheel of Time and new epublished books coming out like that every day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-29-2018, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T12:40:11-07:00","id":1213149,"title":"","content":"The artists have partial control over the IP, but only for the manga. If it gets an anime or video game adaptation the publisher generally controls that part, which can make things pretty tricky. Manga artists sometimes have mixed feelings about adaptations. There are also some horror stories that have arisen due to this system. <br /> <br /> For example, the series Polar Bear's Cafe. One evening the manga author was watching TV, flipped the channel and saw that her manga had been turned into an anime, and then saw that this was episode 20. Nobody had told her, not the editor, the publisher or anyone else that they had greenlit and produced an anime of her manga, let alone that they had already produced 20 episodes. Needless to say she was incredibly upset, and there was a lot of blowback from the community (even those who had never heard of the series) who were angry at how the author had been completely left out of something so important. <br /> <br /> Another series, Negima, was basically cancelled after the publisher openly threatened/bragged aboit taking all the rights away from the manga artist.<br /> <br /> JUMP tends to treat their authors fairly well, all things considered and compared to other publishers but there are a lot of huge problems with the manga industry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-29-2018, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T12:57:24-07:00","id":1213155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213111#post1213111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My issue with Hancock is that at this point in the series, her character and personality is basically just, &quot;I love Luffy a whole lot,&quot; which is unfortunate since she was an interesting character with a pretty dark past. Taking a cool female character and turning her into a one-note comedic love interest irks me. But, to be fair this is One Piece and there are lots of characters (males and females) who are basically one-note, so I'm willing to accept it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if she has been portrayed as comic relief, she's still a bad ass. Don't forget, she was willing to sneak Luffy into the greatest prison system the world government had to offer. And after that, she was willing to attack navy soldiers, as well as pacifistas and Smoker <b>in full view of the public</b> in order to give Luffy the key to Ace's shackles. It's clear she has no problem defying the world government in order to achieve her own ambitions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, I'll agree that it's very difficult to find a female character in most action series that is more than just a support character. The only ones that come to mind right away are magic girl series, and those usually mix in a copious amount of strip tease.<br /> <br /> Oh, actually, there is the Blood series (Blood C, Blood Plus) which features a female as the lead and is set in a horror themed environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-29-2018, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T13:08:35-07:00","id":1213159,"title":"","content":"If you look more towards Seinin series you'll find a bunch with pretty cool, badass action-focused female characters (Black Lagoon, Ghost in the Shell, Witchcraft Works, Jormungand, etc) but it's much harder to find such females in Shounen series which are aimed more at young and adolescent boys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T13:29:12-07:00","id":1213167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213159#post1213159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but it's much harder to find such females in Shounen series which are <b>aimed more at young and adolescent boys.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean... why not ask us to find a live unicorn while we're at it?<br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, what genre is Claymore counted under?<br /> <br /> <br /> And who's the main character of Inuyasha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-29-2018, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T17:37:56-07:00","id":1213238,"title":"","content":"Claymore is shounen (it ran in Shounen Jump) and it's not quite as dark as something like Berserk. Still, I think Claymore definitely pushes some of the boundaries of the Shonen genre, which isn't unusual. There are lots of series that in in shounen magazines that do, like WataMote for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-29-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T19:34:06-07:00","id":1213276,"title":"","content":"I loved claymore until it went off the rails around the time of Miria\u2019s hypothesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T19:54:30-07:00","id":1213286,"title":"","content":"*pops in*<br /> <br /> Oh shit, we have a manga/anime thread? I didn't know that!!!<br /> <br /> *checks in on main topic and sees that it's about...sexism/underrepresented female characters in manga/anime*<br /> <br /> Oh...OH...oh honey...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:10:50-07:00","id":1213295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213286#post1213286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*checks in on main topic and sees that it's about...sexism/underrepresented female characters in manga/anime*<br /> <br /> Oh...OH...oh honey...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just what we're talking about at the moment. If you want to discuss something else, that's cool.<br /> <br /> I'm currently watching Hakume to Mikochi at the moment, which is a series about two tiny little ladies who live in the woods and make friends with animals and such. If anyone ever saw the old series David the Gnome on Nickelodeon back in the day, it's basically a lot like that, only with a few yuri vibes here and there. Also there's a friendly, spooky necromancer who animates dead corpses to do home repair work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:19:56-07:00","id":1213297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213295#post1213295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just what we're talking about at the moment. If you want to discuss something else, that's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even that.<br /> <br /> While discussion on the topic in of itself is fine, but for the purposes of trying to change the anime industry to make it more inclusive? Bit of a dead end.<br /> <br /> Japan seems to want to keep that language and cultural barrier as high as possible with Western fans. That despite the wonders of international simulcasting, the product is ultimately still made by the Japanese and for the Japanese...a first-world country that still remains behind on gender politics, not just in government policy but to even have the conversation in the first place. That they're willing to brush off any criticism and declarations of boycotts as the word of silly Westerners that don't know any better. Or the blunt deflection of &quot;you're going to read/watch/buy it anyways&quot;.<br /> <br /> Japan has to change from within. Not at the behest from those outside of their country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:24:18-07:00","id":1213300,"title":"","content":"Was someone planning a petition?<br /> <br /> I think the conversation, this last week at least, was more about noting the more common problems, not organizing to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Also 'where Naruto got bad or became too much,' which for me was when Sasuke was being trained by Orochimaru after the Sound Four were beaten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-29-2018, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:45:13-07:00","id":1213308,"title":"","content":"I remember back when Toonami first came on Cartoon Network...<br /> <br /> There was not a boy in my school who hadn't memorized the Sailor Moon theme song by heart! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T21:54:31-07:00","id":1213328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1213297#post1213297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Japan seems to want to keep that language and cultural barrier as high as possible with Western fans. That despite the wonders of international simulcasting, the product is ultimately still made by the Japanese and for the Japanese...a first-world country that still remains behind on gender politics, not just in government policy but to even have the conversation in the first place. That they're willing to brush off any criticism and declarations of boycotts as the word of silly Westerners that don't know any better. Or the blunt deflection of &quot;you're going to read/watch/buy it anyways&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so much an anti-western attitude as it is simply a general cultural attitude that encourages more passive resistance than active resistance. For the most part in Japan, they have the attitude of, &quot;If you don't like something, then don't buy it.&quot; If there's a book (or a game or a TV show or a movie or whatever) with material you find offensive or don't like, the attitude is, then just don't spend your money on it, problem solved. Rather than protesting and complaining and boycotting, go find something that you do like and spend your money on that instead. If you can't find something you like, then make it yourself. <br /> <br /> Japanese media has a lot of material that people, even in Japan, find fairly offensive. But rather than trying to boycott or change it, people there just avert their eyes and ignore it. If something starts introducing elements into a series or whatever that a given individual doesn't like, then that person will simply stop following that show or whatever and find something else to watch instead. That's not to say that people don't complain, they certainly do, but they tend not to take communal action or lodge protests with companies or individuals over it. When they do (such as more recently with Kemono Friends and Kadokawa) it tends to be fairly exceptional and is still somewhat frowned on in the overall community. <br /> <br /> This does create something of a cultural gap in Japanese people dealing with American/Western mindsets, where if there's something we don't like or find offensive, we'll complain and boycott the company until they finally change and start making something that no longer offends our sensibilities. Japanese media companies and creators find that attitude incredibly arrogant and it's one of the reasons why many of them aren't terribly keen on doing business with other western countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T13:31:50-07:00","id":1213875,"title":"","content":"It's also a sign of arrogance that we westerners believe that our culture and world views are objectively the right way to live and that the rest of the entire world should be held to the same standard that we place upon ourselves. Basically going into foreign lands and telling them the cultures they've believed in for thousands of years are primitive and evil. You know who else followed that line of reasoning? The Roman Empire, the Crusaders, pretty much anybody who attempted to conquer the world under their banner.<br /> <br /> And then we wonder why most of the outside world hates us...<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------<br /> <br /> Anyways, on to a more happier subject, I went ahead and wrote up some custom Quirks for My Hero Academia!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Rawhide<br /> <b>Type:</b> Mutant<br /> <b>Effects:</b> A primarily defensive type quirk that causes the user's skin to develop into a thick, leathery body armor. This quirk provides the user with increased resistance to damage, but because of their tough skin, it can be difficult to properly treat whatever injuries they do manage to suffer.<br /> <br /> (-)<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Redirection<br /> <b>Type:</b> Emitter<br /> <b>Effects:</b> If utilized to its full potential, this quick can be nearly invincible. It allows the user to alter the vectors of their surrounding environment, changing the direction in which things move, while still retaining its full momentum and power. This quirk's only noticeable weakness is that whatever they're trying to manipulate has to already be in motion, first. If their reaction time is too slow, or they are unaware of an incoming attack, it is possible to bypass the otherwise perfect defense system this quirk provides.<br /> <br /> (-)<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Pardon Me<br /> <b>Type:</b> Emitter<br /> <b>Effects:</b> A quirk that definitely should not be in the hands of the Villain Association, but probably will be anyways. It grants the user a weak form of mind control, which is activated by issuing a formal apology to the person or people you wish to affect. Once under the effects of this quirk's power, the subject will feel compelled to forgive the user of whatever wrongs they feel they've committed. The weakness of this quirk is that it doesn't give the user the freedom to walk around doing whatever they feel like without question. If the user robs a bank and gets caught by the police, they will still have to return the money they stole, but forcing the cops to forgive their transgression may prevent them from being arrested because of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> (-)<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Random Selection<br /> <b>Type:</b> Hybrid<br /> <b>Effects:</b> A versatile, if somewhat unreliable quirk that was created from the combination of a mutant quirk that granted the power of shapeshifting and an emitter quirk which granted the power to duplicate other abilities. The user of this quirk possesses unstable DNA, causing their quirk to fluctuate between powers. Every hour, their current ability is replaced with a different one from a selection of 10 possible options. True to the quirk's name, the choice is completely randomized, with the user having no idea what kind of power they will receive next. The different options provided by this quirk include Enhanced Strength, Rapid Healing, Wings, Retractable Claws, Energy Blasts, Forcefield, Super Speed, Telepathy, Power Dampening and Physical Invulnerability.<br /> <br /> <br /> (-)<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Magnetic Rail<br /> <b>Type:</b> Emitter<br /> <b>Effect:</b> An exceedingly deadly quirk for those specializing in ranged combat. It grants the user the power to create rings of magnetic force, which dramatically accelerates anything attempting to pass through them, much like a rail gun. The weakness of this quick is that the projectile is traveling so blindingly fast, that it is virtually impossible to control its trajectory once it's sent through the ring, so the user must take careful aim before using them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-01-2018, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T13:49:50-07:00","id":1214753,"title":"","content":"Finished watching A Silent Voice and I'd easily recommend it to anyone who likes tragic stories.<br /> <br /> Overlord season 2 was fun but as someone brought up earlier, I'd rather it not have spent so much time on the lizardmen since that level of character building for side characters is generally not suited to the time format anime has in comparison to the light novels being able to extrapolate on small details on and on.<br /> <br /> Hero academia continues to raise the bar despite still having plenty of cliches.<br /> <br /> Violet Evergarden is also a great and tragic story but also has top notch artwork.<br /> <br /> Currently in the middle of steins gate, so far so good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7108-satcom","name":"Satcom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T14:12:24-07:00","id":1214767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satcom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels?p=1214753#post1214753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Overlord season 2 was fun but as someone brought up earlier, I'd rather it not have spent so much time on the lizardmen since that level of character building for side characters is generally not suited to the time format anime has in comparison to the light novels being able to extrapolate on small details on and on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, that's not quite true. We already know that Nazarick is the most powerful force that the New World has ever witnessed. In a straight up fight, there's nobody who can challenge their power. The real threat that Ainz has to worry about is his lack of knowledge regarding the New World. He still doesn't know who used the World Class Item on Shaltear, or what other kinds of WCI's exist in this world. He's actually afraid somebody out there might have possession of a special club that can literally one shot any opponent and said it would be able to destroy the entire guild if used against them.<br /> <br /> The Lizardman Arc was a demonstration in what Ainz has been trying to do, he's researching information about the people of this New World and what they're capable of. We got to see first hand how some of the inhabitants operate, instead of simply hand waving it off camera, and I hope we get to see more arcs like it in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T15:20:21-07:00","id":1215248,"title":"","content":"So I just recently found out about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killing_Bites\" target=\"_blank\">Killing Bites</a> after randomly searching around youtube videos.<br /> <br /> Seems like a pretty interesting series, kind of like the game Bloody Roar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-04-2018, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T11:16:13-07:00","id":1216226,"title":"","content":"To anybody who hasn't read chapter 105 of Attack on Titan yet... brace yourselves for impact... <img src=