watching Tim Burton's 1989 Batman last week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T04:06:59-07:00","id":1520761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2441-lets-talk-anime-manga-visual-novels-light-novels#post2441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I figured I would bring this back. This thread is for the discussion of Anime, Manga, Visual Novels, and Light Novels. I doubt anime and manga need much explanation (Japanese animation and comics). Visual Novels are video games that have very little interaction overall. Its very much a choose your own adventure story. Light Novels are like novellas with periodic pictures. I think Sentai/Kamen Rider/ Toku would be appropriate here.<br /> <br /> Some more basic information: The vast majority of anime do not last more than 26 episodes. Most are only 13 episodes. Anime airs in seasons and rarely is the same show aired back to back (Valverave is an exception, there are some others but its very rare). A common misconception is that all anime is perverted tentacle rape porn or Dragon Ball Z. That's not the case. Anime, Manga, Light Novels and Visual Novels are all just another art medium. The average show is not a 300+ episode monster full of filler and sweaty oily dudes fighting.<br /> <br /> Visual Novels tend to be 18+. They often do have sex scenes in them but many also allow for those to be skipped completely.<br /> <br /> Some Basic Anime Recommendations:<br /> Shounen Battle/Adventire -- Fist of the North Star, JoJo's Bizarre Adventure, Medaka Box, Dog Days, Accel World, Fate/Stay Night, Fate/Zero, Record of Lodoss War (Note that I left off <b>ALL</b> Cartoon Network/Toonami shows)<br /> Comedy -- Lucky Star, Azumanga Daioh, Nichijou, Everyday Lives of Highschool Boys, Genshiken, Lupin III, Maria Holic, Mayo chiki, Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya, Haiyoru! Nyaruko-san, The World God Only Knows, Kamen no Maid Guy<br /> Horror -- Gantz, Another, Monster, Kurozuka<br /> Space Opera/Mecha -- Galaxy 999, Space Pirate Captain Harlock, Space Battleship Yamato 2199, Mobile Suit Gundam (Universal Century stuff), Mouretsu Pirates, Legend of the Galactic Heroes, Giant Robo, Getter Robo, Muv Luv Alternative: Total Eclipse, Ghost in the Shell, Five Star Stories, Neon Genesis Evangelion, Mazinger, Mazinkaiser, Rinne No Lagrange, Macross (Everything ever), AKB0048, Ozma, Zoids<br /> Drama -- Ano Hana, Clannad, Ano Natsu de Materu, Welcome to the NHK, Da Capo, Chobits, Sukitte Ii Na Yo, Kamisama Hajememashita, Inu x Boku SS, Toradora<br /> Seinen -- Berserk, C: The Money of Soul and Possibility, Akira, Spice and Wolf, Bartender, Jormungand, Lupin III, Paranoia Agent, Bakemonogatari, Nisemonogatari, Nekomonogatari, Monogatari S2, Kisemonogatari, Redline, Sankarea, Usagi Drop<br /> Cute Girls/high school/Harem (the only shows that matter) -- Haganai, High School DXD (NSFW), K-On!, Girls und Panzer, Mayo Chiki!, Hyouka, Strike Witches, Tari Tari, Raildex, Upotte!<br /> <br /> Why isn't X on the list? Either I forgot it, haven't seen it, dislike it or its common enough that I don't view it as necessary to add.<br /> <br /> Visual Novel recommendation: Muv Luv, Muv Luv Alternative, Demonbane, Saya no Uta, Chaos;Head, Steins;Gate, Robotic;Notes, Higurashi, Rose Guns Days, Grisai no Kajitsu, Kara no Shoujo, School Days, Da Capo, Otoboku, Little Busters, Clannad, Air,Tsukihime, Fate/Stay Night<br /> <br /> If there is anything I can expand on let me know.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not opposed to Avatar the Last Airrbender or RWBY appearing here but Western Cartoons (Adventure Time, Regular Show, Rugrats, Courage the Cowardly Dog, etc) should get their own thread. Otherwise there will be too much in one thread. I would've left this as just Anime/Manga but VNs and LNs are talked about so rarely here that I didn't see the point in making their own thread so it would just die every few weeks<br /> <br /> Collecting anime posters and <a href=\"https://depositphotos.com/stock-photos/fresh-air.html\" target=\"_blank\">fresh air images</a> has become my passion. The vibrancy of anime art transports me to fantastical worlds, capturing emotions in every brushstroke. Each poster tells a story, and my collection embodies diverse characters and their journeys. On the other hand, curating images of serene landscapes and open skies refreshes my soul. The crispness of the air and the beauty of nature are preserved in each snapshot. Both collections balance my space \u2013 anime fuels creativity, while nature's beauty renews my spirit. In a way, they're visual yin and yang, enriching my surroundings with imagination and tranquility.\u200b<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fan of anime too. Collecting anime posters is like curating a vibrant gallery of imagination and storytelling. Each poster encapsulates a unique world, characters, and emotions that resonate with fans on a personal level. These posters aren't merely decorative; they're windows into beloved series, reminding us of thrilling adventures and heartfelt moments.<br /> <br /> The process of collecting anime posters becomes a journey itself. It's about seeking out rare designs, discovering hidden gems, and connecting with fellow enthusiasts who share the same passion. With each addition, the collection grows into a mosaic of memories, capturing the evolution of personal taste and interests.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","user":"Dazert1","date":". 08-24-2023, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27939-dazert1","name":"Dazert1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27939_1.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T11:34:20-07:00","id":1521208,"title":"","content":"Hubby and I have begun our Naruto rewatch last night. We got through the first five episodes and are falling in love with this series all over again. Believe it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T14:20:34-07:00","id":1521222,"title":"","content":"I started to read Adventures of a Broke Mercenary and I'm somewhat lukewarm to the series thus far and I hope the latter novels w